{"raw": {"https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58959": {"title": "Open Rank Non-Tenure-Line Faculty in Accounting", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Open Rank Non-Tenure-Line Faculty in Accounting Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Open Rank Non-Tenure-Line Faculty in Accounting Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Open Rank Non-Tenure-Line Faculty in Accounting Job Posting Number 2027054APF Job Location San Marcos College/Division McCoy College of Business Department/School Department of Accounting Position Description The Department of Accounting in the Emmett and Miriam McCoy College of Business at Texas State University invites applications for a faculty of practice position (open ranks- assistant, associate, or professor of practice) for Fall 2027. This position requires effective teaching of undergraduate and graduate accounting courses, engagement in applied scholarship, and service to students, the department, the profession, and the university. The position requires the faculty member to teach classes in person. The faculty of practice appointment provides a path for individuals who are entering higher education from established careers in professional practice or management. Required Qualifications Required qualifications for All Ranks: Master\u2019s degree in accounting, law, taxation or a related field from an AACSB accredited institution and active licensure as a CPA ; or a terminal degree (PhD, DBA , or JD) with a major in accounting, taxation, or related field from a school with AACSB or equivalent accreditation. The successful candidate must also possess qualifications required of Scholarly Practitioners (SP) or Instructional Practitioners (IP) under AACSB and Texas State University standards (available at https://www.mccoy.txst.edu/faculty-staff/faculty-resources/policies-procedures/college/cbapps-5-07.html). Required qualifications for Assistant Professor of Practice rank in addition to qualifications listed above for All Ranks: Six years of experience in a professional practice or management role. Required qualifications for Associate Professor of Practice rank in addition to qualifications listed above for All Ranks: Eight years of experience in a professional practice or management role. Significant university teaching experience. Required qualifications for Professor of Practice rank in addition to qualifications listed above for All Ranks: Ten years of experience in a professional practice or management role. Significant university teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability to engage with accounting firms and industry partners and mentor students through the recruitment process. Demonstrated ability to effectively teach undergraduate and graduate accounting courses. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58919 . The confidential review of credentials will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please submit the following before December 31, 2026: Cover letter addressing required and preferred qualifications. Curriculum Vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (All in one document). Teaching evaluations if taught at prior institutions. The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting Universities and letters of recommendation. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 10/19/2026 Review Date 12/31/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58919 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 Evidence of Teaching Experience/Evaluations Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master\u2019s degree in accounting, law, taxation or a related field from an AACSB accredited institution and active licensure as a CPA; or a terminal degree (PhD, DBA, or JD) with a major in accounting, taxation, or related field from a school with AACSB or equivalent accreditation? Yes No * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Professor * Do you possess qualifications required of Scholarly Practitioners (SP) or Instructional Practitioners (IP) under AACSB and Texas State University standards (available at https://www.mccoy.txst.edu/faculty-staff/faculty-resources/policies-procedures/college/cbapps-5-07.html)? Yes No * Do you have at least six years of experience in a professional practice or management role? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58949": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Reading Education", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant or Associate Professor of Reading Education Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant or Associate Professor of Reading Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Reading Education Job Posting Number 2027033TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Education Department Curriculum And Instruction Position Description The D epartment of Curriculum and Instruction at Texas State University invites applications for one full-time, nine-month faculty position in Reading Education. The position may be filled at the rank of tenure-track Assistant Professor or Associate Professor with tenure, with appointment beginning Fall 2027. We seek a scholar with a clearly identifiable program of research focused on reading instruction, assessment, and intervention. This faculty member will teach undergraduate and graduate literacy and reading methods courses for teacher and reading specialist candidates in programs leading to Texas teacher certification. The successful candidate will demonstrate expertise in evidence-based literacy practices that reflect the linguistic variation, demographics, and educational needs of Texas educators and students, including multilingual populations. This position requires excellence in teaching, active scholarly engagement, and meaningful service to the program, department, college, university, and profession. The faculty member will contribute to accreditation, curriculum development, and continuous improvement efforts consistent with the Texas Education Agency ( TEA ) and other accreditation standards. Appointment at the Associate Professor rank will require meeting Texas State University and Department of Curriculum and Instruction standards for appointment with tenure. RESPONSIBILITIES Key responsibilities for this position are structured across four core domain areas: Teaching & Field Supervision: Teach undergraduate and graduate reading/literacy courses, including topics related to literacy including reading assessment and intervention, and reading methods. Supervise field experiences and support clinical practice placements across partner school districts. Utilize evidence-based, student-centered instructional practices responsive to wide ranging learner needs. Curriculum & Assessment: Lead and support literacy curriculum development aligned with the Texas Essential Knowledge and Skills ( TEKS ) in English Language Arts and Reading ( ELAR ), English Language Proficiency Standards ( ELPS ), Response to Intervention / Multi-Tiered Systems of Support ( RTI / MTSS ), Science of Reading frameworks, and other state guidelines. Participate in assessment of student learning outcomes and overall program effectiveness. Contribute to accreditation reporting and continuous improvement processes. Research & Scholarly Activity: Maintain an active, high-quality research agenda in reading and literacy education. Publish scholarly research in peer-reviewed journals and present regularly at state, national, and international professional conferences. Seek external research funding and grant opportunities when appropriate. Service & Leadership: Serve actively on program, departmental, college, and university committees. Participate in school-university partnerships and community literacy initiatives. Contribute to program governance, student advising, and strategic planning. Support professional literacy organizations and academic journals as a reviewer, editor, or committee leader. ABOUT US Housed in the Department of Curriculum and Instruction, Texas State University\u2019s Reading Education program prepares initial teacher candidates and certified educators across elementary, middle, and secondary school settings. Alongside its graduate degree and Reading Specialist certification tracks, the program actively supports undergraduate initial teacher education by delivering foundational reading methods and assessment-driven literacy instruction. Aligned with International Literacy Association ( ILA ) and Texas Education Agency ( TEA ) standards, the program equips candidates to design and implement evidence-based reading instruction, assess language and literacy development, and support culturally and linguistically varied learners. Ultimately, the overall aim of the program is to advance student literacy outcomes across Texas and beyond by cultivating reflective teacher-scholars who engage in field-based research, curriculum development, and school-wide literacy leadership. Additional information about the program can be found here: https://www.education.txst.edu/ci/reading-education-masters.html and more details on the department is available at: https://www.education.txst.edu/ci/ Required Qualifications Assistant Professor: Earned doctorate in Reading/Literacy Education or a directly related field from an accredited institution of higher education (conferred by appointment date). Demonstrated expertise in teaching children and/or adolescents how to read. Knowledge of (or a clear commitment to learning) Texas literacy mandates, educational policies, standards, and literacy instruction for wide populations, including multilingual learners, alongside an understanding of broader state or national literacy contexts. Evidence of three (3) or more years of successful PK-12 teaching experience in ELAR . Evidence of successful higher education teaching experience or strong potential for high-quality university instruction. Emerging record of scholarly activity and peer-reviewed publication. Demonstrated commitment to preparing educators to effectively support all learners. Associate Professor: Applicants seeking appointment at the Associate Professor rank must hold an earned doctorate in Reading/Literacy Education or a directly related field from an accredited institution, meet all required qualifications for the Assistant Professor rank, and in addition demonstrate: Record of sustained, high-quality higher education teaching at both undergraduate and graduate levels. Record of sustained, high-impact peer-reviewed scholarly activity focused in reading education. Record of active, meaningful professional, institutional, and community service. Accomplishments sufficient to meet Texas State University and Department of Curriculum and Instruction standards for appointment at the Associate Professor rank with tenure. Preferred Qualifications Assistant Professor: Knowledge of psychometrics and reading assessment frameworks and demonstrated ability to use assessment knowledge and resulting data to inform instructional decisions. Direct experience in reading assessment for the general education classroom to guide instruction in Tier 1 and beyond. Direct experience in clinical and/or school-based intervention. Possess depth and breadth of knowledge in reading research, varied foundational frameworks and approaches including Science of Reading, with an understanding of their relationship to the broader landscape of literacy research, perspectives and pedagogical practices. University teaching experience in reading education or a closely related field. Experience teaching and/or supervising teacher candidates and reading specialist candidates. Experience delivering effective instruction across in-person, hybrid, and online modalities. Experience integrating educational technology into literacy instruction. Associate Professor: Deep knowledge of psychometrics and reading assessment methodologies. Extensive experience conducting reading assessment and intervention in school or clinical settings. Evidence of successful teaching and supervision of teacher and reading specialist candidates. Evidence of successful teaching across in-person, hybrid, and online delivery modalities. Evidence of successful integration of educational technology into literacy instruction. Evidence of successful grant writing or leadership in funded research projects. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University online employment portal will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58786 . To ensure full consideration, complete application packages should be submitted by December 15, 2026. Required submission materials include: Addressing required and preferred qualifications for rank, describing research agenda, scholarly goals, approach to teaching, and contributions to teacher preparation. Comprehensive CV detailing educational background, academic positions, publications, presentations, grants, and service. Two (2) samples of scholarly writing (e.g., peer-reviewed journal articles, manuscripts under review, or dissertation chapter). Student evaluations, peer teaching evaluations, or a summary portfolio demonstrating university instructional effectiveness. Unofficial transcripts from all degree-granting higher education institutions. As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide information about the applicant\u2019s skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. Candidates selected for hire will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 10/19/2026 Review Date 12/15/2026 Close Date 12/15/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58786 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Writing Sample Evidence of Teaching Experience/Evaluations Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctorate in developmental literacy, reading or a closely related field at time of application? Yes, I do have a PhD in developmental literacy, reading or a closely related No, I do not * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58948": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Topology", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant or Associate Professor in Topology Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant or Associate Professor in Topology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor in Topology Job Posting Number 2027032TTL Job Location Round Rock, San Marcos College/Division College of Science and Engineering Department Mathematics Position Description The Department of Mathematics at Texas State University is seeking to hire a tenure-track assistant professor or associate professor with tenure, with a research specialization in topology, starting Fall 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain a high-quality research program in topology. The candidate must also be dedicated to the teaching and mentoring of students at the graduate and undergraduate levels. In addition, the candidate will be expected to be actively engaged in service to the department, college, university, and mathematical community. The Department of Mathematics is a growing department with a broad range of strengths in Analysis, Topology, Algebra, Combinatorics, and Statistics, Applied Mathematics, Logic, and Mathematics Education. The department started its new Ph.D. program in Mathematics in Fall 2025 to complement its Ph.D. program in Mathematics Education and its master\u2019s programs. The faculty has over $3 million in active grants, including multiple NSF CAREER awardees (one faculty working in topology). The Department strives to create a welcoming environment that invites students from a wide range of backgrounds to major in mathematics, statistics, and data science. We invite applicants who are enthusiastic about mentoring students at the undergraduate and graduate levels to reach their potential. The Department is dedicated to the success of its junior faculty, providing support through formal mentoring, reduced teaching and service loads, collaboration and collegiality, and opportunities to participate in university-wide professional development programs. Texas State University is in San Marcos, a city 25 miles south of Austin and 50 miles north of San Antonio. San Marcos consistently ranks as a fast-growing community in the United States. Nestled in the Texas Hill Country and in the middle of Texas\u2019 innovation corridor, the campus enjoys a beautiful setting along the banks of the San Marcos River. Texas State University is dedicated to teaching and research excellence, and the university\u2019s \u201cRun to R1\u201d program aims to support faculty to lift the university to R1 status by supporting research and grant activities. Texas State University has been named by Forbes as a Best Employer, and Best Employer for Women. Texas State University is a member of The Texas State University System and is a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution ( HSI ). The Austin-San Antonio area has many opportunities for collaborations outside of the university and an increasing demand for expertise in mathematics, statistics, and data analysis. Major companies such as Dell, Tesla, Google, IBM , AMD , and Apple have a large presence in the Austin area. San Antonio is home to USM and Rackspace and is a center for healthcare and biosciences. Many of our faculty have collaborations with industry and nearby universities. Required Qualifications Assistant Professor: An earned doctorate in mathematics, or a closely related field prior to employment. Evidence of, or potential for, research excellence in topology. Assessment will focus on recent publications. Evidence of excellence in teaching and ability to teach both undergraduate and graduate level mathematical courses. Evidence of, or potential for, mentoring and advising PhD students in the topology concentration. A strong preparation in mathematics. An ability to contribute to the departmental mission. Associate Professor: An established research agenda and publication record. Experience in teaching and mentoring students at all levels, as well as evidence of service to their department, university, and the broader community. For this position, we expect the candidate to have earned tenure in a department of mathematics with similar standards as Texas State University. Preferred Qualifications Potential for research collaboration with current faculty. Evidence of, or potential to, obtain external funding. Application Procedures Applicants must submit the following via https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/29257 : Cover letter. AMS cover sheet. Curriculum vitae. Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts (all in one document). Statement of research agenda. Statement of teaching philosophy. Three letters of recommendation with at least one addressing teaching. Additionally, applicants must submit the following on this site: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58903 . Curriculum vitae. Cover letter. Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts (all in one document). To ensure full consideration, all materials listed above should arrive at the required locations by Tuesday, November 10, 2026. However, we shall continue to accept applications until the position is filled. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 10/19/2026 Review Date 11/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58903 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctorate in mathematics, applied mathematics, statistics, or a closely related field or anticipate completion prior to start date? Yes, I have an earned doctorate in mathematics, applied mathematics, statistics, or a closely related field. Yes, I anticipate completing a doctorate in mathematics, applied mathematics, statistics, or a closely related field prior to start date. No. * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58946": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Postdoctoral Scholar Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Postdoctoral Scholar Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Postdoctoral Scholar Job Posting Number 2027053APF Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Applied Arts Department/School Dept of Organization, Workforce, & Leadership Studies Position Description This postdoctoral scholar position supports NSF -funded research focused on STEM and computer science education, with an emphasis on mixed methods, , and community-engaged research. The scholar will contribute to research, teaching, mentoring, and service activities in collaboration with the ACCEYSS Research Group and partner institutions. Dr. Shetay Ashford-Hanserd, Professor in the Department of Organization, Workforce, and Leadership Studies at Texas State University, seeks a postdoctoral scholar with mixed methods research experience in STEM or computer science education to join the ACCEYSS Research Group. This position is supported by a research grant from the National Science Foundation and focuses on mixed method empirical research. The ideal candidate will be self-motivated, detail-oriented, and experienced in mixed-methods, preferably including graduate coursework in mixed-methods research. Priority will be given to candidates with experience related to mixed-method data analysis methods and approaches. The initial appointment will be for one year and may be renewed for up to three years, contingent on continued funding availability. Assist with project management, mixed-methods data collection and analysis, manuscript preparation, and dissemination of research findings. Conduct STEM+C education and workforce research. Facilitate research group meetings, conferences, and workshops with collaborating researchers from Universities in Texas and Florida. Visit and conduct research in collaboration with community partners and gain experience conducting community-engaged, participatory STEM+C research. Teaching: Serve as an instructor of record of undergraduate and graduate courses in interdisciplinary studies, STEM and/or computer science education. Train team members on mixed-methods research methodology. Teach courses online, on campus (San Marcos or Round Rock), and off campus. Mentor undergraduate researchers in a service-learning course. Supervise interdisciplinary internships, practicums, and research projects. Service: Engage in activities at the department, college, and university level that build relationships with other university departments, local businesses, and community organizations as well as participating in professional organizations. Engage in service activities with education, STEM and computer science, professional and academic organizations. Required Qualifications Earned doctorate degree in education, engineering education, computer science education, STEM education, workforce development, interdisciplinary studies, or related field by appointment date. Evidence of mixed-method research experience. Experience teaching students in online and on-campus environments. Demonstrated ability to foster collaborative relationships with stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications Training in mixed-method research. Experience conducting a mixed-method study. Teaching experience in higher education. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University faculty employment website will be considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58802 . Interested individuals should submit the following documents in the requested document sections: A cover letter detailing their research interests and relevant experience. A current curriculum vitae (CV). A statement of teaching philosophy. Examples of recent publications. Comprehensive research agenda. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). As part of the application process, you will be asked to provide 3 references in the reference letter section. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date 11/01/2026 Posting Date 10/19/2026 Review Date 10/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58802 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Examples of Recent Publications Comprehensive Research Agenda Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you or will you earn your doctorate degree in education, engineering education, computer science education, STEM education, workforce development, interdisciplinary studies, or a related field by appointment date? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Diverse Issues in Higher Education InsightintoDiversity.com Texas Workforce Commission-Work in Texas Colleague, friend, and/or personal referral Other (Please Specify in follow up question below) * Please Specify: (enter \"NA\" if not applicable) (Open Ended Question) * Official transcripts are required for all degrees that provide evidence of a faculty member's credentials and qualifications. Foreign/International transcripts for all degrees must undergo a credentialing evaluation for U.S. equivalency by an organization that is a member of the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES). If selected for hire, I will provide official transcripts and/or evaluations for all degrees earned. Yes No * Are you currently eligible to work in the United States of America? Yes. No. * Do you now or will you in the future require a petition for a H1B employment visa? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58941": {"title": "Assistant Professor - School of Criminal Justice and Criminology", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor - School of Criminal Justice and Criminology Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor - School of Criminal Justice and Criminology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor - School of Criminal Justice and Criminology Job Posting Number 2027031TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Applied Arts Department School of Criminal Justice and Criminology Position Description The School of Criminal Justice and Criminology at Texas State University invites applicants for up to two full-time (nine-month) tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin in Fall 2027 . Responsibilities include high-quality research, undergraduate and graduate level teaching, and university, professional, and community service. Salary is negotiable and commensurate with experience. The selected candidate will be required to submit to a background check and provide official transcripts from all degree-granting universities. All positions are subject to availability of funds. Required Qualifications Earned (or anticipate earning by the beginning of the Fall 2027 semester) a Ph.D. in Criminal Justice, Criminology, or related field; those who hold only a JD will not be considered. Evidence or potential of peer-reviewed publication and ability to sustain publication productivity. Preferred Qualifications Have strong methodological/analytic skills. Can contribute to the growth and versatility of the School\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs. Have potential for seeking and/or securing external grant funding. Have evidence of effective teaching. Demonstrate a commitment to service and student mentorship. Application Procedures Only applications submitted for this specific posting through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58514 . For full consideration please submit the following materials: Cover letter that addresses all required and preferred qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). A sample of publishable or published work. The names and contact information for three references. Inquiries about this position may be directed to Dr. Elisa Toman, Search Committee Chair, at etoman@txstate.edu Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 10/16/2026 Review Date 10/28/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58514 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Samples of Scholarly Work/Research Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in criminal justice, criminology, or related field or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have a Ph.D. in criminal justice, criminology, or related field. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58931": {"title": "Open Rank Tenure Line in Engineering Management", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Open Rank Tenure Line in Engineering Management Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Open Rank Tenure Line in Engineering Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Open Rank Tenure Line in Engineering Management Job Posting Number 2027030TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Science and Engineering Department Department of Engineering Technology Position Description The Department of Engineering Technology invites applications for a research faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in Engineering Management. This position is designed for individuals whose primary focus is on research, scholarly, and creative activities that enhance the research mission of the university, with a strong emphasis on mentoring and supervising PhD students. The successful candidate will play a critical role in supporting doctoral student progression, including dissertation development, research design, and publication. The position carries expectations for actively mentoring doctoral students in their own research throughout their academic journey; conducting externally funded research producing high-impact scholarly work; and teaching graduate level courses. Responsibilities Mentor and supervise PhD students, including dissertation advising and research development. Contribute to the growth and structure of the PhD program in Engineering Management. Support doctoral students through key milestones, including proposal development, research execution, and publication. Develop and sustain an independent, externally funded research program. Lead and manage research teams that include graduate and doctoral students. Publish in high-impact, peer-reviewed journals. Collaborate with faculty, industry, and external research partners. Required Qualifications For all ranks: Earned doctoral degree in engineering, engineering management, operations research, analytics, management science, or a closely related field. Demonstrated research competence and scholarly contributions. Evidence of research productivity, including peer-reviewed publications. Demonstrated ability or strong potential to mentor graduate and PhD students. Excellent Oral and Written English Language skills. For Associate Professor: Minimum of five years of independent, externally funded research experience. Demonstrated record of sustained scholarly contributions. Experience mentoring graduate or doctoral students. For Professor: Minimum of ten years of independent, externally funded research experience. Demonstrated national or international recognition in the field. Significant experience mentoring PhD students and supervising dissertation work. Record of leadership in research programs and professional organizations. Preferred Qualifications Experience graduating doctoral students or serving on dissertation committees. Established record of securing external funding. Experience leading interdisciplinary or industry-sponsored research. Alignment with Engineering Management research areas such as analytics, risk, operations, or decision-making. Teaching and mentoring students in an online environment. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered, https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings To be considered for the position, applicants are required to submit the following application materials: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Research Statement. Teaching Philosophy. Three reference letters, (at least) one of which explicitly addressing teaching. To ensure full consideration, all materials listed above should arrive by November 15, 2026 . Please clearly address how you meet all criteria in your application materials. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 10/13/2026 Review Date 11/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57917 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a doctoral degree in an engineering or management (with an industrial focus) discipline? Yes, I have a doctoral degree in an engineering or management (with an industrial focus) discipline. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Professor Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58930": {"title": "Assistant Professor in the History of US Foreign Relations since 1898", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in the History of US Foreign Relations since 1898 Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor in the History of US Foreign Relations since 1898 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor in the History of US Foreign Relations since 1898 Job Posting Number 2027026TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department History Position Description The Department of History at Texas State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in United States foreign relations since 1898. The successful candidate will be expected to teach survey courses in United States history and specialized undergraduate and graduate courses in US foreign relations, to direct graduate theses and serve on graduate committees, and to participate actively in departmental programs, service, and governance. Required Qualifications A PhD in History or a related fields required by the time of appointment. Candidates must demonstrate an active research agenda in the History of US Foreign Relations. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with the potential to contribute to Applied History and to those who demonstrate an active research agenda with a scholarship record that complements the existing strengths of the History Department. Application Procedures Appointment date August 16, 2027, salary is commensurate with experience. To guarantee full consideration, application materials must be received by November 6, 2026 . Only applications submitted for this specific posting through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58692 . A complete application includes: A cover letter. A CV. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Three letters of recommendation. A writing sample. For further questions please contact Search Committee Chair Dr. Sarah Coleman, sarahcoleman@txstate.edu . Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 10/06/2026 Review Date 11/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58692 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Writing Sample Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in history or related field or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have a Ph.D. in history or related field. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58927": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction \u2013 Elementary Education", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Instruction \u2013 Elementary Education Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Instruction \u2013 Elementary Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Instruction \u2013 Elementary Education Job Posting Number 2027052APF Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Education Department/School Curriculum And Instruction Position Description The Department of Curriculum and Instruction seeks to find the ideal candidate to serve as an Assistant Professor of Instruction in Elementary Education with a focus on English as a Second Language ( ESL ) and Early childhood education ( ECE ). The responsibilities for this position include teaching four classes per semester and overseeing field-based experiences for university students in a local elementary school and/or early childhood center. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in an education-related field of study from an accredited university. Teacher certification. A minimum of 3 years of teaching experience in PK-12 schools. Evidence of being current in the field of ESL instruction, ECE instruction, ELAR instruction, teacher preparation, research-based best practices and pedagogies. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in an education-related field of study from an accredited university. Experience supervising preservice teachers in field-based experiences in Texas. Experience teaching in higher education. Experience preparing teachers for ESL certification in Texas. Experience teaching in a bilingual or dual language classroom. Application Procedures Only applications submitted for this specific posting through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58663 . Interested individuals should submit the following materials: A current CV. A letter of interest outlining specific academic and professional experiences relevant for appointment. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide information about the applicant\u2019s skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. Candidates selected for hire will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Date 10/16/2026 Review Date 10/23/2026 Close Date 10/23/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58663 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master\u2019s degree in an education-related field of study from an accredited university? Yes, I have a master's degree in a related field No * How many years of teaching experience do you have at the university level? No prior teaching experience. Less than 1 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years or more * Describe your prior teaching experience (if any) including experience teaching classes that are delivered face-to-face, online, or remotely. Include a list of all classes taught. (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58926": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Instruction Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Instruction Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Instruction Job Posting Number 2027051APF Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Applied Arts Department/School Dept of Organization, Workforce, & Leadership Studies Position Description The Department of Organization, Workforce, and Leadership Studies ( OWLS ) at Texas State University is seeking an exemplary and visionary Lecturer to join us in preparing reflective and driven leaders to thrive in today\u2019s global workforce. The Assistant Professor of Instruction position is a full-time, non-tenure-track, nine-month appointment based at the San Marcos campus, with additional responsibilities to serve as BAAS Program Coordinator. The position is primarily a teaching and service appointment, with a 3/1 workload: three courses per long semester plus one course equivalent assigned to BAAS program coordination. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, teaching core courses that are integral to the Bachelor of Applied Arts and Sciences ( BAAS ) degree program and related high demand focus areas and providing leadership for the BAAS program. Specific duties include: Teach undergraduate courses in the OWLS Department in an online, in-person, or hybrid delivery system. Travel to in-person recruitment events as needed. Work non-traditional hours, including evenings, nights, and Saturdays. Lead teaching and recruitment activities for the BAAS program. Attend and present at university events, including Bobcat Day, welcome events, graduation celebrations, commencement, academic advisor workshops, presentations to undergraduate Admissions staff and Athletics staff, and meetings with new advisors to promote the BAAS degree. Take part in undergraduate curriculum updates. As BAAS Program Coordinator, working in consultation with the Department Chair: Collaborate with Texas Global on AOP development and expansion. Provide ongoing support for AOP implementation, course scheduling, and program improvement. Manage per-course faculty tasks. Review new student files for appropriateness of transfer coursework to be added to the degree modules. Monitor program and course enrollments. Manage undergraduate learning outcomes. Manage student issues and keep the Department Chair informed of pertinent student concerns. Support BAAS updates, including the undergraduate catalog description, Transfer Planning Guides, brochures, information documents and flyers, the BAAS Student Handbook, sample course sheets, and the BAAS program website. Support updates to Canvas course sites. Coordinate scheduling of OWLS undergraduate courses and instructor assignments. Provide student services in recruiting, registration, academic advising, developing and individualizing degree plans, identifying career goals, reviewing petitions to change degree plans, preparing for capstone, and working with former students when they are readmitted. Serve as liaison to community colleges and businesses by attending events and responding to inquiries. Serve as the BAAS liaison and contact person for student referrals across the university. Collaborate with department leadership and administrative staff. Coordinate BAAS student learning outcome reporting process. An ideal candidate will show evidence of outstanding teaching in higher education and the ability to lead BAAS program coordination. All positions are subject to availability of funds. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in interdisciplinary studies, education, management of technical education, training and development, leadership, organization development, human resources, student affairs, online learning, counseling, administration, or a related field from a regionally accredited university or equivalent. Experience teaching online or hybrid/blended format at the university level or documented training in teaching online. Higher education teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate preferred. Experience working with non-traditional learners in a higher education setting, which could include advising or teaching. Experience with online curriculum development in Canvas. Experience with academic advising at university or college level. Experience with analysis and planning of academic learning outcomes. Experience recruiting students. Three or more years in higher education teaching experience at a university or college. Demonstrated commitment to culturally responsive practices and culturally relevant instruction. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58778 . To ensure full consideration, please submit the following materials by 10/25/2026 : Current curriculum vitae. Cover letter describing experience and fit with the position. List of three academic/professional references including phone numbers and email addresses. A brief statement of teaching philosophy regarding teaching non-traditional students in online and hybrid format and recruitment of students. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Optional two letters of recommendation. The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting universities and pass a background check. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date 01/01/2027 Posting Date 10/16/2026 Review Date 10/26/2026 Close Date 10/25/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58778 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have earned a Master\u2019s degree in interdisciplinary studies, education, management of technical education, training and development, leadership, organization development, human resources, student affairs, online learning, counseling, administration, or a related field from a regionally accredited university or equivalent by the end of this year (2026)? Yes, I have or will have a master\u2019s in interdisciplinary studies, education, management of technical education, training & development, leadership, organization development, human resources, student affairs, online learning, counseling, administration, or No - (disqualifying) * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Diverse Issues in Higher Education InsightintoDiversity.com Texas Workforce Commission-Work in Texas Colleague, friend, and/or personal referral Other (Please Specify in follow up question below) * Official transcripts are required for all degrees that provide evidence of a faculty member's credentials and qualifications. Foreign/International transcripts for all degrees must undergo a credentialing evaluation for U.S. equivalency by an organization that is a member of the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES). If selected for hire, I will provide official transcripts and/or evaluations for all degrees earned. Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58925": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Translational Health Research Center", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Translational Health Research Center Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Translational Health Research Center Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Translational Health Research Center Job Posting Number 2027050APF Job Location San Marcos College/Division Division of Research Department/School Translational Health Research Center Position Description Translational Health Research Center ( THRC ) seeks to develop a pool of candidates for one- and two-year postdoctoral positions (postdocs) at an interdisciplinary university-level research center. THRC seeks to foster healthy and resilient people and places through research conducted by Texas State investigators, along with corporate and community partners. THRC postdocs gain broad, interdisciplinary knowledge and skills working on applied research and community-based interventions. Faculty mentors from multiple academic disciplines work with postdocs on Texas State\u2019s campuses in San Marcos and/or Round Rock, Texas. THRC postdocs engage in research and professional training opportunities related to topics such as community health and resilience, interprofessional health practice, health journalism and data visualization, health economics, team science, digital health technology, AI and health informatics, dissemination and implementation science, rural and telehealth innovation, and related areas of inquiry. A postdoc is a professional research appointment designed to provide recent doctoral degree recipients with additional experiences and skills to advance their careers. Each THRC postdoc develops an individualized training plan ( ITP ) in collaboration with faculty mentors The ITP serves as a roadmap for various research responsibilities and outcomes associated with the postdoc\u2019s appointment. It also includes information about various professional development and networking opportunities that will be available to THRC postdocs during their appointment. The Translational Health Research Center will accept applications from qualified applicants on a continual basis. Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool postdoc position will be available for consideration in case the need arises. Required Qualifications Recently awarded a Ph.D. in health or social sciences, business, communication, or applied STEM field. Recent health-related research experience. Preferred Qualifications Experience with interdisciplinary, team, and/or community-based research. Application Procedures Applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58751 . Interested individuals should submit: A current CV . A letter of interest outlining specific academic and professional experiences relevant for a postdoc research appointment with the Translational Health Research Center. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). A statement of research interest. The CV should also include the names and contact information for three academic references who can provide information about the applicant\u2019s research skills and experiences. The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from the highest degree granting institution. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date Posting Date 10/16/2026 Review Date 10/30/2026 Close Date 04/05/2027 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58751 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Samples of Scholarly Work/Research Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in health or social sciences, business, communication, or applied STEM field or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I earned a Ph.D. in health or social sciences, business, communication, or applied STEM field. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. * What are your areas of research interest that align with the position? (Open Ended Question) * What is the title of your dissertation? (Open Ended Question) * Official transcripts are required for all degrees that provide evidence of a faculty member's credentials and qualifications. Foreign/International transcripts for all degrees must undergo a credentialing evaluation for U.S. equivalency by an organization that is a member of the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES). If selected for hire, I will provide official transcripts and/or evaluations for all degrees earned. Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Diverse Issues in Higher Education InsightintoDiversity.com Texas Workforce Commission-Work in Texas Colleague, friend, and/or personal referral Other (Please Specify in follow up question below) Please Specify: (enter \"NA\" if not applicable) (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58885": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Health Administration", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant or Associate Professor, Health Administration Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant or Associate Professor, Health Administration Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor, Health Administration Job Posting Number 2027002TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Health Professions Department School of Health Administration Position Description The College of Health Professions School of Health Administration ( SOHA ) Texas State University ( TXST ), invites applications for one assistant or associate rank tenure-track position. This is a full-time, in-person position located at the San Marcos campus, with a nine-month appointment to begin Fall 2027. Salary will be commensurate with the candidate\u2019s experience and qualifications. Candidates are expected to actively pursue and maintain an externally funded research program.This position is second of two new FTEs available within SOHA for a Tenure Track faculty member with a teaching and research interest in health information technology/health information management. This position is subject to the availability of funds. Required Qualifications Required qualifications for all ranks: An earned doctorate and masters. One degree must be in healthcare administration or closely related field. One degree must be from CAHME , AACSB or CePH accredited program. Required qualifications for rank of Assistant Professor , in addition to those required above: Strong interpersonal communication and leadership skills.Commitment to excellence in teaching and learning consistent with the program vision, mission, and goals. Established publication history. Established research agenda. Required qualifications for rank of Associate Professor, in addition to those required above: Minimum five years teaching experience. Established research publication history. Established external funding record. Demonstrated teaching excellence and service leadership accomplishments. Preferred Qualifications Preferred qualifications for all ranks: Board certification or board certification eligible and plan to seek certification in the American College of Healthcare Executives ( ACHE ), Healthcare Financial Management Association ( HFMA ), American College of Health Care Administrators ( ACHCA ), American College of Medical Practice Executives ( ACMPE ), American Health Information Management Association ( AHIMA ), or other appropriate professional organization related to the field of healthcare administration.Industry experience in the healthcare domain (ideally in a series of positions of increasing responsibility). As this is an in-person position, the candidate must have a willingness to teach on campus. synchronous classes.Previous record of funded external grant activity and peer-reviewed publications. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56711 . To ensure full consideration please submit the following before January 14, 2027: Cover Letter that addresses all required and preferred qualifications. Curriculum Vitae. Two Letters of Recommendation. Samples of Scholarly work or research. Evidence of Teaching experience or evaluations. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting Universities. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 07/08/2026 Review Date 01/14/2027 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/56711 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Samples of Scholarly Work/Research Evidence of Teaching Experience/Evaluations Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Licensure Certifications Letter of Recommendation #2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Professor * Do you have an earned masters or doctorate, one of which must be in healthcare administration or closely related field from a CAHME, AACSB or CePH accredited program? Yes, I have an earned masters or doctorate degree, one of which must be in healthcare administration or closely related field from a CAHME, AACSB or CePH accredited program. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? The Chronicle of Higher Education InsideHigherEd.com HigherEdJobs.com Diverse Issues in Higher Education InsightintoDiversity.com Texas Workforce Commission-Work in Texas Colleague, friend, and/or personal referral Other (Please Specify in follow up question below) * Official transcripts are required for all degrees that provide evidence of a faculty member's credentials and qualifications. Foreign/International transcripts for all degrees must undergo a credentialing evaluation for U.S. equivalency by an organization that is a member of the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES). If selected for hire, I will provide official transcripts and/or evaluations for all degrees earned. Yes No * Are you currently eligible to work in the United States of America? Yes. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58830": {"title": "Open Rank in Aging &amp; Dementia Research", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Open Rank in Aging &amp; Dementia Research Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Open Rank in Aging & Dementia Research Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Open Rank in Aging & Dementia Research Job Posting Number 2027029TTL Job Location San Marcos, Round Rock College/Division Department Office of the Provost and EVPAA Position Description Texas State University seeks applications for open-rank professor positions to conduct research on any aspect of aging and dementia research. Texas State University is a leader in aging and dementia with strengths in interdisciplinary social and behavioral dementia research, translational and community-engaged research, caregiving, ethics and autonomy in aging, environmental research and community design, physical therapy and cognitive psychology. Texas State is home to a robust community already working across disciplines, the Alliance of Researchers in Aging ( ARIA ). ARIA supports networking opportunities and interdisciplinary research in aging, including research on cognition, cognitive decline and dementia, mental health, care-giving, and physical, social and spiritual well-being. Texas State also offers a Master of Science degree in Dementia and Aging Studies with three tracks: 1) Dementia and Long-Term Care, 2) Practitioner and 3) Researcher. Texas State University receives a full share of the Texas University Fund ( TUF ) and plans to invest funds in recruitment and substantial start-up support for strategic hires with established research programs and active external funding in historic and emerging areas of research strength, including in aging and dementia research. Texas State University hosted a town hall on April 8 to discuss areas of impact for hiring in aging and dementia research and to bring together the aging and dementia research community. We seek to hire dynamic and innovative scholars with strong research records supported by external funding. An applicant\u2019s scholarly focus should complement and enhance the aging and dementia scholarship and teaching strengths of Texas State and the strengths of the Endowed Chair in Aging and Dementia. Responsibilities: Bring and seek external funding and coordinate interdisciplinary grants with both internal and external collaborators. Conduct and publish original research on aging and dementia. Lead interdisciplinary collaboration with faculty across the university. Develop and maintain an active research agenda. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses on aging and dementia, and related subjects. Mentor and advise students. Contribute to the workforce development and development of the aging and dementia curriculum. Participate in service activities at the department, college, and university levels. The successful candidate will join the department(s) appropriate to their area of scholarly focus. Required Qualifications Ph.D. or terminal degree Evidence of a strong scholarly focus on and sustained record of research excellence in aging and dementia research Evidence of sustained record of excellence in teaching and mentoring students. Evidence of a sustained record of obtaining external funding. The successful applicant will receive the appropriate rank and title based on university and department established standards. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of activity in organizing conferences and sessions on aging and dementia Experience in teaching and mentoring both undergraduate and graduate students Experience supporting experiential learning for undergraduate and graduate students Strong commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration Evidence of community engagement for scholarship and teaching Application Procedures Applications will be considered on a rolling basis. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58499 . Interested applicants should submit the following materials: A cover letter highlighting scholarly focus, publications, teaching, and external funding. A detailed curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). The names and contact information of three references. The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Proposed Start Date August 16, 2027 Posting Date 10/09/2026 Review Date 10/16/2026 Close Date 10/16/2026 Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58499 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) List of References Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctoral degree or terminal degree from an accredited institution or international equivalent? Yes, I earned a doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution or international equivalent. No, I do not have a doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution or international equivalent. * Summarize your external funding record for the past ten years. Include award titles, agencies, funding amounts, your role, and key outcomes (e.g., publications, products, student training). (Open Ended Question) * Describe the way your research and teaching would complement and enhance the aging and dementia scholarship and teaching strengths of Texas State and the strengths of the Endowed Chair in Aging and Dementia. (Open Ended Question) * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Professor Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58795": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Ancient Mediterranean History, 500 BCE-500 CE", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in Ancient Mediterranean History, 500 BCE-500 CE Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor in Ancient Mediterranean History, 500 BCE-500 CE Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Ancient Mediterranean History, 500 BCE-500 CE Job Posting Number 2027027TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department History Position Description The Department of History at Texas State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor with a research focus on Ancient Mediterranean History between 500 BCE and 500 CE. The successful candidate will be expected to teach survey courses in ancient Greek and Roman history, the first half of Western or World Civilization, and specialized undergraduate and graduate courses on their research area. The successful candidate will also be expected to develop new undergraduate and graduate courses and participate in graduate committees. Participation in departmental programs, service, and governance is expected. Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in Ancient History or related field is required by the time of appointment. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with experience in Applied History or Digital Humanities, and to those who demonstrate an active research agenda with a scholarship record that complements the existing strengths of the History Department. Application Procedures The appointment date is August 16, 2027 . Salary is commensurate with experience. All positions are subject to availability of funds. To guarantee full consideration, application materials must be received by November 6, 2026 . Only applications submitted for this specific posting through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58697 . A complete application includes: A letter of application addressing the candidate\u2019s research agenda and how they would approach teaching Ancient history to Texas State\u2019s student population. A CV. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Three letters of recommendation. A sample syllabus of an introductory class to the Greek and Roman worlds (one document). For any other questions please contact Search Committee Chair, Dr. Jos\u00e9 Carlos de la Puente, jd65@txstate.edu . Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 10/06/2026 Review Date 11/06/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58697 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Syllabi Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in history or related field or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have a Ph.D. in history or related field. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58766": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Management", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Management Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Management Job Posting Number 2027028TTL Job Location Round Rock, San Marcos College/Division Department Department of Management Position Description The Department of Management in the McCoy College of Business at Texas State University invites applications for a recently approved, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin in Fall 2027. The successful candidate for this position will regularly publish high-quality research in the management/supply chain domain. A successful candidate will also teach undergraduate and/or graduate management/supply chain courses while engaging in service appropriate for this rank. Additionally, a successful candidate will have an interest in supporting initiatives of the university, college, and department. About the Department of Management The Department of Management is a highly collegial and intellectually vibrant group of approximately 41 full-time faculty. The department offers a B.B.A. in Management (with concentrations in Entrepreneurial Studies, Human Resources, Leadership and Decision-Making, and Supply Chain Management); offers a university-wide minor in Innovation & Entrepreneurship; supports the college\u2019s face-to-face and online M.B.A. programs as well as the college\u2019s D.B.A. program; and serves as the home of the Center for Student Entrepreneurship. About the McCoy College of Business The McCoy College of Business provides student-centered undergraduate, master\u2019s, and doctoral programs that produce graduates with the skills and experience to compete responsibly, professionally, and successfully in dynamic business environments. Nationally acclaimed faculty, extraordinary community partners, and industrious students collaborate to solve business challenges through applied research. As an AACSB -accredited institution with over 6,700 students, the McCoy College of Business emphasizes innovation, experiential learning, student-focused engagement, research, and service as it educates the next generation of global business leaders. The McCoy College of Business is home to the #1 Sales Program (worldwide), ranked #4 in family business research productivity (United States), ranked among the Top 30 Best Business Schools (among US public universities), and offers a Tier 1 MBA program. In recent years, the part-time MBA program was ranked among the best part-time MBA programs in the nation by U.S. News & World Report. About Texas State University Texas State University , located along the beautiful San Marcos River, is in the center of the Texas Innovation Corridor. The city of San Marcos is home to the university, which is 25 miles south of Austin and 60 miles north of San Antonio. Nestled in the Texas Hill Country, the campus enjoys a beautiful setting along the banks of the San Marcos River and nearby access to two major airports. Texas State is driving what\u2019s next in research, academic excellence, and student success. The promising students, inspiring faculty, dedicated staff, and new graduates are primed to have an impact, change lives, and make a difference in the world. As a national research university with a Carnegie classification of Doctoral University: High Research Activity, Texas State is committed to world-class research and scholarly activities that span all disciplines, create new knowledge, and advance economic, cultural, and technological progress to address real-world issues. Texas State is on a trajectory to become a \u201cTier One\u201d research university. With more than 48,000 students, Texas State is among the 50 largest public universities in the nation. Students choose from over 200 bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs offered by nine colleges. Texas State\u2019s enrollment of minority students accounts for over 50% of the student population, and Hispanic-student enrollment accounts for over 35% of the student body. The university is a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution and is one of 30 institutions nationally to receive the prestigious Seal of Excelencia in recognition of efforts to accelerate the success of Hispanic students in higher education. Additionally, Texas State has been named by Forbes as a Best Employer, and Best Employer for Women. The university is also regularly ranked as a Best College for Veterans. Additional Details about the Position The following details are offered as general information to applicants. Please note that the information below is subject to change. Salary: The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications. Location: San Marcos campus (while the majority of courses are taught at the San Marcos campus, there may be a future need for teaching at the Round Rock campus). Support: Includes the potential for summer support, other research support, and a professional development budget for research use and conference attendance. Other Information about Why to Choose Texas State: https://www.hr.txst.edu/talent-acquisition/why-choose-txst.html Benefits: Numerous benefits are offered (see https://www.hr.txst.edu/benefits.html for an overview). The Department of Management seeks a collegial faculty member to advance the department and college as the university transitions to a top-tier research institution while maintaining a strong commitment to teaching. Candidates with supply chain management expertise and interests in emerging areas such as AI applications in supply chain are encouraged to apply. This position is subject to the availability of funds. Required Qualifications Successful applicants must possess the following qualifications: A Ph.D. in Supply Chain, Business Administration, or a related business field, from an AACSB -accredited institution by the date of hire. A history of, or strong potential for, publishing in high-quality, peer-reviewed business journals commensurate with rank. Experience in high-quality teaching of Supply Chain Management courses at the undergraduate or graduate level commensurate with rank. A record of service commensurate with rank. Preferred Qualifications Successful applicants may also possess the following desirable qualifications: Evidence of publishing in top-tier scholarly business journals, according to the Australian Business Deans Council ( ABDC ) Journal Quality List or the Chartered Association of Business Schools ( CABS ) Academic Journal Guide. Evidence of high-quality teaching of Supply Chain Management or related courses (include a summary of teaching evaluations). Evidence of a research interest in Supply Chain Management. Evidence of a commitment to high-quality professional and institutional service activities. Evidence of related industry experience. Application Procedures Only applications submitted for this specific posting through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58684 . To ensure full consideration, please submit the following by 11/5/2026 : Cover letter (that clearly describes how each required qualification is met). Curriculum vitae with references. Research statement (that details research program and goals). Evidence of teaching effectiveness (a summary of teaching evaluations is preferred). Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting universities. Questions may be directed to Dr. Indu Ramachandran, Search Committee Chair (i_r38@txstate.edu) Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 10/06/2026 Review Date 11/06/2026 Close Date 11/05/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58684 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Research Interests Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in supply chain management, business, management, or a related field from an AACSB-accredited institution? Yes, I have a Ph.D. in supply chain management, business, management, or a related field from an AACSB-accredited institution. No, I do not have a Ph.D. in supply chain management, business, management, or a related field from an AACSB-accredited institution. Yes, ABD with a completion date prior to start. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58765": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction in Social Work and Assistant Professor of Instruction in Social Work / Program Coordinator", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Instruction in Social Work and Assistant Professor of Instruction in Social Work / Program Coordinator Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Instruction in Social Work and Assistant Professor of Instruction in Social Work / Program Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Instruction in Social Work and Assistant Professor of Instruction in Social Work / Program Coordinator Job Posting Number 2027048APF Job Location Round Rock College/Division College of Applied Arts Department/School School of Social Work Position Description Texas State University School of Social Work invites applications for two full-time, nine-month, non-tenure line faculty positions at the Assistant Professor of Instruction rank. The positions include: (1) Assistant Professor of Instruction and (2) Assistant Professor of Instruction/Program Coordinator. Both positions will be based at the University\u2019s Round Rock Campus and they will teach in-person classes during the day or in the evening. Both positions will contribute to the School of Social Work\u2019s academic mission through high-quality teaching, student engagement, and service. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate social work courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats, as assigned, and participating in appropriate service activities at the School, College, University, professional, and community levels. Required Qualifications Assistant Professor of Instruction: MSW or DSW required or equivalent with two years\u2019 experience. Prior teaching experience or related. Assistant Professor of Instruction / Program Coordinator: MSW or DSW required or equivalent with two years\u2019 experience. Prior Leadership / Supervisory Experience. Prior teaching experience or related. Preferred Qualifications Assistant Professor of Instruction: Doctoral degree, preferably in social work. Current, valid, and unencumbered social work license. Experience with electronic learning management systems. Demonstrated evidence of campus and community engagement. One year plus teaching experience. Two years of experience in social work practice or related fields. Assistant Professor of Instruction / Program Coordinator: Doctoral degree, preferably in social work. Current, valid, and unencumbered social work license. Experience with electronic learning management system. Demonstrated evidence of campus and community engagement. Two years of experience in social work practice or related fields. One year plus teaching experience. Application Procedures To ensure full consideration, please submit the following by October 26, 2026. Only applications submitted for this specific posting through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58705 . To ensure full consideration, please submit the following A current curriculum vitae (CV). A cover letter that clearly identifies the position of interest while describing experience and fit with both the required and preferred aspects of the position. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). A statement of the applicants teaching philosophy. Three references from which we may request letters of recommendation if the applicant is selected for an interview. Selected candidates for interview will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date January 6, 2027 Posting Date 10/06/2026 Review Date 10/26/2026 Close Date 10/26/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58705 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in social work or related field or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have a Ph.D. in social work or related field. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. * Please indicate whether you wish to be considered for the program coordinator role. Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58757": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor Job Posting Number 2027025TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Political Science Position Description The Department of Political Science invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level, beginning Fall 2027, to teach required and elective graduate and undergraduate courses in Public Administration. The Department awards the Bachelor of Public Administration degree and the Master of Public Administration degree. Applicants must be able and willing to teach undergraduate and graduate public administration courses in San Marcos and Round Rock, Texas, including day and evening courses. The successful candidate will also be expected to teach and develop courses in the core public administration curriculum in in-person, fully online, hybrid, and accelerated formats. For information on Texas State faculty appointment policy, please visit: http://policies.txstate.edu/division-policies/academic-affairs/04-01-23.html. All positions are subject to fund availability. Required Qualifications Earned Ph.D. in public administration or a related field from an accredited university at the time of appointment. Potential for, or a record of, research and scholarly publication in public policy and administration. Demonstrated ability or potential to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in public administration and public policy, including in-person, fully online, hybrid, and accelerated formats. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching or developing undergraduate and/or graduate courses, or demonstrated willingness to develop courses, in one or more of the following core areas: organization theory, public personnel administration, public law, policy processes, ethics, research methods or research design, and program evaluation. Experience teaching courses in person, fully online, in hybrid formats, and/or in accelerated formats across the public administration curriculum. Experience or proficiency with learning management systems (e.g., Canvas), video conferencing (e.g., Zoom), spreadsheets, databases, and data analysis. Relevant experience presenting at professional public administration conferences, seminars, and workshops. Experience writing, submitting, and administering grants. Knowledge or experience working in diverse, multicultural, and international environments. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58729 . To assure full consideration, please submit the following before November 13, 2026 : A Cover Letter outlining professional experience. Resume or Current Curriculum Vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). Course teaching evaluations (if available). Note that as part of our application process, we also request contacts for three references. Please provide the names and email addresses for your references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. Upon submission of your application, an automated email will be generated and sent to your references with instructions on how to attach the reference letter to your application through a confidential online portal. Candidates selected for interviews will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Inquiries about this position may be directed to Ms. Alexis Finley, Administrative Assistant, Department of Political Science at xui25@txstate.edu or 512-408-3772. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 10/06/2026 Review Date 11/16/2026 Close Date 11/13/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58729 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you earned a Ph.D. in Public Administration or a related field from an accredited university or will have acquired one at the time of appointment? Yes, I have or will have my Ph.D. degree in public administration or a related field from an accredited university at the time of appointment. No, I do not/will not have my Ph.D. degree in public administration or a related field from an accredited university at the time of appointment. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58756": {"title": "Open Rank Faculty in Special Education", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Open Rank Faculty in Special Education Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Open Rank Faculty in Special Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Open Rank Faculty in Special Education Job Posting Number 2027024TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Curriculum And Instruction Position Description The Department of Curriculum and Instruction at Texas State University invites applications for one full-time, nine-month faculty position in Special Education. The position may be filled at the rank of tenure-track Assistant Professor or Associate Professor with tenure, or Professor with tenure beginning fall 2027. We seek a scholar with a clearly identifiable program of research focused on Special Education and improving educational opportunities and outcomes for individuals with disabilities. The successful candidate should be able to contribute to teaching across multiple Special Education program areas (i.e., Special Education generalist). Candidates from all areas of Special Education are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will contribute to the undergraduate and graduate Special Education programs and to the preparation of Special Education teachers and other professionals who serve individuals with disabilities. The candidate will teach courses at the undergraduate and graduate level, maintain an active program of research, advise and mentor students, contribute to program development, and provide service and leadership within the program, department, university, and profession. Courses are offered on campus, hybrid, and online (synchronous and asynchronous) during the day and in the evening. Appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor rank will require meeting Texas State University and Department of Curriculum and Instruction standards for appointment with tenure. RESPONSIBILITIES Key responsibilities include: Teaching undergraduate and graduate Special Education courses, including courses supporting teacher preparation and certification, across in-person, hybrid, and online modalities; developing or revising courses as program needs arise. Supervising teacher candidates in field-based or clinical teaching experiences. Maintaining an active and focused program of research that results in peer-reviewed publications and professional presentations. Seeking external funding to support research and/or personnel-preparation activities, as appropriate. Advising and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Contributing to the continued development and improvement of the Special Education programs. Supporting program activities related to educator preparation, state requirements, accreditation, and alignment to professional standards. Providing service and leadership to the Special Education program, Department of Curriculum and Instruction, College of Education, university, and profession. ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT The Department of Curriculum and Instruction is located within the College of Education at Texas State University. The department offers undergraduate and graduate programs that prepare educators and other professionals to support learning and student success across educational settings. Additional information about the Department of Curriculum and Instruction is available at https://www.education.txst.edu/ci/ . Required Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS : ASSISTANT PROFESSOR Earned doctorate in Special Education or a closely related field from an accredited institution by the start date. Applicants who are completing their dissertations may apply but must have the degree conferred by the start date of August 16, 2027. A clearly identifiable program of research focused on Special Education or the education of individuals with disabilities. Evidence of peer-reviewed scholarly productivity. Evidence of effective university teaching. Evidence of the ability to contribute to undergraduate and graduate Special Education programs, including Special Education teacher preparation. Three or more years of professional experience in PK\u201312 educational settings supporting students with disabilities or other specialized learning needs, such as experience as a Special Education teacher, school psychologist, dyslexia specialist, educational diagnostician, behavior specialist, or in a comparable role. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS : ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR or PROFESSOR Applicants seeking appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor rank must hold the current rank of Associate of Professor, an earned doctorate in Special Education or a closely related field from an accredited institution and meet all other required qualifications for Assistant Professor, as well as the following: A clearly identifiable and sustained program of research focused on Special Education or the education of individuals with disabilities. A record of sustained peer-reviewed scholarly productivity. A record of effective university teaching. A record of contributing to Special Education teacher preparation or other educator-preparation programs. A record of professional service. Current rank of Associate Professor or Professor Accomplishments sufficient to meet Texas State University and Department of Curriculum and Instruction standards for appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor rank with tenure. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS : ASSISTANT PROFESSOR University teaching experience in Special Education or a closely related area. Evidence of potential for securing external funding for research or personnel preparation. Experience contributing to educator-preparation or teacher-certification programs. Experience developing or participating in partnerships with schools, districts, or other educational organizations. Evidence of potential for mentoring graduate students. Possession of one or more professional certifications, licenses, or specialized credentials relevant to Special Education or related services (e.g., Board Certified Behavior Analyst, Certified Academic Language Therapist, transition-related certification, National Board Certification, or a comparable credential). PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS : ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR or PROFESSOR A record of securing external funding for research or personnel preparation. Experience mentoring and advising graduate students and serving on graduate committees. Experience providing leadership in educator preparation, program development, accreditation, or teacher certification. Experience developing and sustaining partnerships with schools, districts, educational agencies, or professional organizations. Possession of one or more professional certifications, licenses, or specialized credentials relevant to Special Education or related services (e.g., Board Certified Behavior Analyst, Certified Academic Language Therapist, transition-related certification, National Board Certification, or a comparable credential). Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University employment website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58712 . To ensure full consideration, applicants should submit the following by November 18, 2026 : A cover letter addressing the required and preferred qualifications for the applicable rank. The letter should describe the applicant\u2019s program of research and future scholarly goals, approach to university teaching, and potential contributions to Special Education teacher preparation. A current curriculum vitae. Two samples of scholarly writing. If applicable, teaching evaluations from the last two years (when assigned as teacher of record). Unofficial transcripts from all degree-granting institutions. As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide information about the applicant\u2019s skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. The selected candidate will ultimately be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting institutions. Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 10/06/2026 Review Date 11/18/2026 Close Date 11/18/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58712 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Scholarly Writing Sample Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Experience/Evaluations DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a earned doctorate in Behavior Analysis, Special Education, Psychology, or a closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have an earned doctorate in Behavior Analysis, Special Education, Psychology, or a closely related field from an accredited institution of higher education. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Professor Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58752": {"title": "Nontenured Faculty Pool - International Affairs (TSIE)", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Nontenured Faculty Pool - International Affairs (TSIE) Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Nontenured Faculty Pool - International Affairs (TSIE) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Nontenured Faculty Pool - International Affairs (TSIE) Job Posting Number 2027041NTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division TXST Global Division Department/School International Affairs Position Description The Office of International Affair\u2019s Texas State Intensive English Program seeks to develop a pool of candidates for possible temporary/nontenured faculty to teach Intensive English courses. Teaching appointments will be made on an as-needed basis, one level per term, determined by program enrollment and departmental need. Appointment entails approximately 20 hours per week for a duration of 8 weeks. Responsibilities: Teach one TSIE level, delivering engaging and level-appropriate English language instruction. Adapt and develop instructional materials in alignment with TSIE program objectives Maintain consistent communication with students, fostering a supportive and positive learning environment. Utilize assigned or approved syllabi and assessment tools (where available), tailoring content to meet specified Student Learning Outcomes (SLOs). Provide timely, constructive feedback on assignments and assessments. Evaluate students based on established SLOs and submit final grades, comments, and pass/fail notifications by stipulated deadlines. Demonstrate professional attire (business casual) and demeanor while promoting a collegial environment among students and colleagues. Fulfill course-related administrative duties, as required by TSIE . Temporary/nontenured faculty are appointed to teach one to four courses per semester. Teaching appointments are based upon student demand on a semester-by-semester basis. Eligibility for annual reappointment is contingent upon satisfactory annual performance evaluations during the term period, in addition to continuity of funding and departmental need. Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool faculty position will be available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. This posting is for the Fall 2025, Spring 2026, and Summer 2026 semesters. Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool faculty position will be available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arise and funding is subject to availability. Required Qualifications A BA or Certificate in TESOL is required. College level teaching experiences. Native-like English language proficiency. Demonstrated excellence in teaching ESL (e.g., teaching evaluations). Preferred Qualifications Masters in TESOL or related field. Prior teaching experience in an intensive English program or an academic ESL / EFL program. Application Procedures The Texas State Intensive English Program will accept applications from qualified applicants on a continual basis. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58357 . Interested individuals should submit the following: Current CV. Letter of interest outlining specific academic and professional experiences relevant for appointment. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Optional: Syllabi. Teaching statement. As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide information about the applicant\u2019s skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. Candidates selected for hire will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Type of Position Part-Time Proposed Start Date Posting Date 09/18/2026 Review Date 05/31/2027 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58357 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Syllabi Teaching Statement Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of teaching experience do you have at the university level? No prior teaching experience. Less than 1 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years or more * Describe your prior teaching experience (if any) including experience teaching classes that are delivered face-to-face, online, or remotely. Include a list of all classes taught. (Open Ended Question) * Official transcripts are required for all degrees that provide evidence of a faculty member's credentials and qualifications. Foreign/International transcripts for all degrees must undergo a credentialing evaluation for U.S. equivalency by an organization that is a member of the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES). If selected for hire, I will provide official transcripts and/or evaluations for all degrees earned. Yes No * What is your schedule availability? Days/Nights; Days of the Week; Location (e.g., San Marcos, Round Rock, online courses, etc.) (Open Ended Question) * Which semester(s) do you wish to be considered for? Fall, Spring, Summer or Combination? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58727": {"title": "Faculty of Practice or of Instruction - Concrete Industry Management", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Faculty of Practice or of Instruction - Concrete Industry Management Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Faculty of Practice or of Instruction - Concrete Industry Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Faculty of Practice or of Instruction - Concrete Industry Management Job Posting Number 2027047APF Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Science and Engineering Department/School Department of Engineering Technology Position Description The Department of Engineering Technology at Texas State University has one Open Rank Non-tenure line ( NTL ) vacancy in either a Faculty of Practice or Faculty of Instruction appointment for the expanding Concrete Industry Management ( CIM ) program. The CIM Program is a hands-on discipline that combines principles of construction management, materials science, and business within a comprehensive and in-demand degree program that is widely supported by the concrete industry. The successful candidate will be expected to teach relevant undergraduate courses for students preparing for a career in the concrete materials/construction industry or related careers; work with student organizations and/or mentor student competition teams; travel with students to industry conferences locally, nationally, and internationally; develop and maintain relationships with concrete industry companies; participate in membership in industry associations that represent the concrete and construction industries; and participate in service activities in support of the university, the department, and the profession. Workload for NTL faculty includes teaching, at a minimum, 12 credits each semester per area of expertise and department needs and fulfilling service and advising obligations each semester. Applicants with expertise in all areas related to concrete production or concrete construction management are invited to apply. Required Qualifications For all ranks: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Concrete Industry Management, Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, or a related field. Excellent oral and written English language skills. For Faculty of Practice, all ranks: At least five years of experience in the concrete or construction industry including plant management, operations management, project management and coordination, jobsite supervision/management, subcontracting, or other applicable concrete or construction industry related experience. Current and contemporary competence in professional practice or management. Scholarship through professional presentations, publications, or similar contributions. For the rank of Associate Professor of Practice: Minimum of 10 years of experience in the concrete or construction industry including plant management, operations management, project management and coordination, jobsite supervision/management, subcontracting, or other applicable concrete or construction industry related experience. Demonstrated leadership in relevant professional organizations. For the rank of Professor of Practice: Minimum of 15 years of experience in the concrete or construction industry including plant management, operations management, project management and coordination, jobsite supervision/management, subcontracting, or other applicable concrete or construction industry related experience. Documented recognition by peers for professional contributions to the field (e.g. awards). For Faculty of Instruction, all ranks: Current and contemporary competence in their teaching content area. Potential for continued professional growth in teaching and instructional activities. For the rank of Associate Professor of Instruction: At least five years of full-time effective teaching and learning contributions, including advances in curriculum, pedagogy, course delivery, or similar innovation. Potential for increased leadership in teaching and instructional activities (e.g., course coordination, teaching innovation, professional outreach, scholarly engagement). For the rank of Professor of Instruction: The requirements listed for Associate Professor of Instruction. At least 10 years of full-time effective and sustained teaching and learning contributions, including advances in curriculum, pedagogy, course delivery, or similar innovation. Documented recognition for leadership and contributions in teaching and instructional activities (e.g., awards, accreditation reviews, curriculum innovation, program coordination, scholarly contributions). Preferred Qualifications Masters or Doctoral degree in Concrete Industry Management, Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, or a related field. Higher education teaching experience as an instructor or guest lecturer. University level teaching experience in construction or concrete industry management or related programs. Construction and/or concrete industry certifications or professional licensure (i.e. American Institute of Constructors ( AIC ) Associate Constructor (AC), or Certified Professional Constructor ( CPC ), Construction Management Association of America ( CMAA ) Certified Construction Manager ( CCM ), Project Management Institute Construction Professional ( PMI -CP), professional engineer (PE), registered architect, or other certifications related to the construction profession such as LEED -AP and OSHA Authorized Trainer. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58374 . To assure full consideration, submit the following before 15 November 2026 : A cover letter. A curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Statement of teaching philosophy. Evidence of teaching experience and evaluation. List of at least three references. Selected candidates for interview will be required to provide transcripts from all degree granting universities. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 10/02/2026 Review Date 11/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58374 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Evidence of Teaching Experience/Evaluations Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Concrete Industry Management, Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, or related field? Yes. I have a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Concrete Industry Management, Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, or related field. No, I do not have a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Concrete Industry Management, Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, or related field. * Please select the rank you are applying for: Associate Professor of Practice Professor of Practice Associate Professor of Instruction Professor of Instruction Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58726": {"title": "Faculty of Practice or of Instruction - Construction Management", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Faculty of Practice or of Instruction - Construction Management Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Faculty of Practice or of Instruction - Construction Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Faculty of Practice or of Instruction - Construction Management Job Posting Number 2027046APF Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Science and Engineering Department/School Department of Engineering Technology Position Description The Department of Engineering Technology at Texas State University is seeking applicants to fill a non-tenure track position at the rank of Professor, Associate Professor, or Assistant Professor in our growing Construction Science and Management ( CSM ) and Concrete Industry Management ( CIM ) programs, beginning in Fall 2026. These undergraduate programs are accredited by the American Council for Construction Education ( ACCE ) and the Association of Technology, Management and Applied Technology ( ATMAE ), respectively, and currently serve about 1000 students. The department is also home to MS and PhD programs in construction management with in-person and online options. While candidates with expertise in all areas of construction management will be considered, preference will be given to those in the areas of heavy civil, highway and/or industrial construction. The successful candidate will be expected to teach relevant undergraduate courses for students preparing for a career in the construction industry or related careers; work with student organizations and/or mentor student competition teams; develop and maintain relationships with construction industry companies; participate in relevant industry associations; and participate in service activities in support of the university, the department, and the profession. Workload for NTL faculty includes teaching 12 credits each semester in the area of expertise and based on department needs, and fulfilling service and advising obligations each semester. The preferred start date for this position is about 8/15/2027 to allow for a successful applicant to begin teaching in the fall semester 2027. Required Qualifications For all ranks: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, Concrete Industry Management, or a related field. Excellent oral and written English language skills. For Faculty of Practice, all ranks: At least five years of experience in the construction industry including heavy highway, heavy civil, or industrial construction; project management and coordination, jobsite supervision/management, subcontracting, or other applicable construction industry related experience. Current and contemporary competence in professional practice or management. Scholarship through professional presentations, publications, or similar contributions. For the rank of Associate Professor of Practice: Minimum of 10 years of experience in the construction industry. Demonstrated leadership in relevant professional organizations. For the rank of Professor of Practice: Minimum of 15 years of experience in the construction industry. Documented recognition by peers for professional contributions to the field (e.g. awards). For Faculty of Instruction, all ranks: Current and contemporary competence in their teaching content area. Potential for continued professional growth in teaching and instructional activities. For the rank of Associate Professor of Instruction: At least five years of full-time effective teaching and learning contributions, including advances in curriculum, pedagogy, course delivery, or similar innovation. Potential for increased leadership in teaching and instructional activities (e.g., course coordination, teaching innovation, professional outreach, scholarly engagement). For the rank of Professor of Instruction: The requirements listed for Associate Professor of Instruction. At least 10 years of full-time effective and sustained teaching and learning contributions, including advances in curriculum, pedagogy, course delivery, or similar innovation. Documented recognition for leadership and contributions in teaching and instructional activities (e.g., awards, accreditation reviews, curriculum innovation, program coordination, scholarly contributions). Preferred Qualifications Masters or Doctoral degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, Concrete Industry Management, or related field. Higher education teaching experience as an instructor or guest lecturer. University level teaching experience in construction management or related programs. Construction and/or concrete industry certifications or professional licensure (i.e. American Institute of Constructors ( AIC ) Associate Constructor (AC), or Certified Professional Constructor ( CPC ), Construction Management Association of America ( CMAA ) Certified Construction Manager ( CCM ), Project Management Institute Construction Professional ( PMI -CP), professional engineer (PE), registered architect, or other certifications related to the construction profession such as LEED -AP and OSHA Authorized Trainer. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58373 . To assure full consideration, submit the following before 1 November 2026 : A cover letter. A curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Statement of teaching philosophy. Evidence of teaching experience and evaluation. List of at least three references. Selected candidates for interview will be required to provide transcripts from all degree granting universities. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 10/02/2026 Review Date 11/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58373 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Evidence of Teaching Experience/Evaluations Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Concrete Industry Management, Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, or related field? Yes. I have a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Concrete Industry Management, Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, or related field. No, I do not have a Bachelor\u2019s degree in Concrete Industry Management, Construction Management, Construction Engineering Technology, Construction Engineering, or related field. * Please select the rank you are applying for: Associate Professor of Practice Professor of Practice Associate Professor of Instruction Professor of Instruction Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58723": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Trumpet", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Trumpet Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Trumpet Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Trumpet Job Posting Number 2027022TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department School of Music Position Description The School of Music at Texas State University seeks an engaging, creative, collaborative, and dedicated teacher/performer to serve as a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Trumpet. Duties begin August 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to: Teach undergraduate and graduate applied trumpet, trumpet literature and pedagogy courses, coach chamber and trumpet ensembles, and other topics according to the candidate\u2019s qualifications and the needs of the School of Music. Maintain a record of scholarly/creative activity and make substantive professional contributions to the field of trumpet performance and pedagogy. Participate in faculty meetings, committees, and service activities. Recruit and retain a full studio of undergraduate and graduate trumpet students. Fulfill other duties assigned by the Director of the School of Music. Required Qualifications Doctorate in trumpet performance or related field (must be completed by August 15, 2027), or equivalent professional experience. Evidence of excellence in trumpet teaching at the professional or collegiate level. Demonstrated record of achievement in scholarly/creative activities and potential for further professional growth. \u00b7 Ability to perform in a variety of musical styles and genres. Potential for success in student recruitment. Experience working with individuals from varied backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications University teaching experience. National/international stature as a trumpet player. Demonstrated communication and organizational skills, and an ability to work collaboratively. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58581 . Interested individuals should submit the following: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Statement of Teaching Philosophy Contact information (name, title, mailing address, phone number, and email address) for three references. Links to a minimum of three performance videos as a solo performer or solo and ensemble performer from the past three years. Videos should demonstrate varied styles and should be edited, if necessary, so as not to exceed 30 minutes total. Link to a teaching demonstration video from the past three years, totaling no more than 15-20 minutes. Video should provide full view of teacher and student in a typical trumpet lesson Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). Proposed Start Date August 15, 2027 Posting Date 09/29/2026 Review Date 10/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58581 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy URL - Video File URL - Teaching Video Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Resume Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 Other Required Documents List of References Additional URL Additional URL#2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a DMA in trumpet performance or related field, or equivalent professional experience? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58689": {"title": "Director, School of Music", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Director, School of Music Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Director, School of Music Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Director, School of Music Job Posting Number 2027023TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department School of Music Position Description Texas State University, a Hispanic-Serving Institution ( HSI ) located in San Marcos, Texas, invites applications for the position of Director of the School of Music . With more than 47,000 students, Texas State is one of the 25 largest public universities in the U.S., as well as one of the fastest growing institutions in the nation. With a key goal of elevating student success, the university offers over 200 bachelor\u2019s, master\u2019s, and doctoral degree programs across nine colleges. The university is a federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution and is one of 30 institutions nationally to receive the prestigious Seal of Excelencia in recognition of efforts to accelerate the success of Hispanic students in higher education. Additionally, Forbes has named Texas State among America\u2019s Best Colleges in 2026, as well as previous recognitions among America\u2019s Best Employers. U.S. News and World Report named Texas State among the Best Global Universities, and multiple degree programs rank among the best in the world including programs in drama, nursing, business, and criminology. Texas State University\u2019s 693-acre San Marcos campus resides in the center of Texas\u2019s innovation corridor. Nestled in the Texas Hill Country, the campus enjoys a beautiful setting along the banks of the San Marcos River and nearby access to two major airports (Austin and San Antonio). Texas State University also operates the 101-acre campus in Round Rock, Texas north of Austin, as well as over 4,000 additional acres of academic, agricultural, research, and recreational spaces across Texas. In 2025, TXST launched its first international campus located in Quer\u00e9taro, Mexico. Originally founded in 1899, Texas State is now driving what\u2019s next in research, academic excellence, and student success. The promising students, inspiring faculty, dedicated staff, and new graduates are primed to create an impact, transform lives, and make a difference in the world. The Texas State University School of Music is a long-standing, fully accredited member of the National Association of Schools of Music and provides an intensive and nurturing environment that emphasizes student-faculty interaction. Ninety faculty teach more than 600 students who perform in more than thirty ensembles. We guide students to become performers, educators, and scholars through a comprehensive array of degree programs. Graduate degrees include the Master of Music in Music Education, and the Master of Music with a concentration in Choral Conducting, Composition, Digital Music Research, Instrumental Conducting, Musicology, Music Theory, Performance and Pedagogy, and Performance in multiple genres including Classical, Jazz, Mariachi, and Salsa. Graduate students may also pursue a Certificate in Music Performance. In addition to a Bachelor of Arts in Music and a Bachelor of Science in Sound Recording Technology, undergraduate degrees include the Bachelor of Music in Music Education (Band, Choral, Mariachi, Strings) and Performance (classical and jazz). Composition, Jazz, Mariachi, Music, and Opera are available as Minors. Additional information can be found at https://www.music.txstate.edu . The Director is the chief executive officer of the School of Music, responsible to the Dean of the College of Fine Arts and Communication for all matters concerning budget, programs, and faculty of the school. The successful candidate is expected to: Foster an environment that values shared governance, educational excellence, collaboration, innovation, a variety of perspectives, and a welcoming community. Support and promote the continuing growth and development of outstanding academic curricula in undergraduate and graduate programs. Provide vision and dynamic leadership for the engagement of faculty, staff, and students in the continued pursuit of excellence. Expand resources by working with University Advancement. Actively advocate for the school across campus and with constituents outside the University. Recruit, retain, and develop a varied and high-quality faculty by supporting creative/scholarly research, collaborative partnerships, and external funding efforts. Manage the administrative affairs of the school, including management of a large and complex budget. Contribute to the continued development and success of the school through leadership in research, teaching, and service. For more information about the functions of school directors at Texas State, visit https://policies.txst.edu/division-policies/academic-affairs/01-02-11.html . Required Qualifications Doctoral/Terminal degree or equivalent professional experience. Record of significant teaching and scholarly/performance activities in music that merit appointment with tenure at the rank of Professor. Demonstrated relevant administrative leadership in higher education or a multifaceted arts organization. Demonstrated commitment to transparent communication and collaborative decision-making that will foster shared governance. Preferred Qualifications DMA , Ph.D. or terminal degree in Music or related field. Significant administrative experience with an academic unit offering a comprehensive spectrum of academic and professional programs in music. Demonstrated ability to manage budgets, facilities, and personnel. Familiarity with NASM standards and procedures. Demonstrated success in advocating for resources with internal and external constituents, including but not limited to donor cultivation, alumni engagement, and fundraising, with a focus on building student scholarship support. An informed understanding of the changing landscape of music, including contemporary modes of creation, production, performance, distribution, audience engagement, and interdisciplinary collaboration. A track record of building trust and community and fostering faculty/staff mentorship. Demonstrated experience in promoting recruitment and success of faculty, staff, and students. Application Procedures For full consideration, applications should be received by November 11, 2026 . The position will remain open until filled. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered, https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58609 . Interested individuals should submit the following: A letter of application that includes a detailed and supported explanation of how you meet the qualifications for this position and your vision for the future of the school. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of no more than two pages, presenting your leadership philosophy, including but not limited to the themes of shared governance, administrative transparency, faculty development, and departmental community building. Applicants must upload a single reference document that includes the names, professional titles, organizations, email addresses, and phone numbers of five professional references who can speak to the applicant\u2019s qualifications and experience. Reference letters are not required at the time of application. Phone reference checks will be conducted for top candidates as part of the evaluation process. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 09/29/2026 Review Date 11/11/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58609 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Leadership statement List of References Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a doctoral/terminal degree or equivalent professional experience? Yes, I have a doctoral/terminal degree. Yes, I have equivalent professional experience. No, I do not have a doctoral/terminal degree or equivalent professional experience. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58687": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction in Music Education (Music Education and Student Teaching Coordinator)", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Instruction in Music Education (Music Education and Student Teaching Coordinator) Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Instruction in Music Education (Music Education and Student Teaching Coordinator) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Instruction in Music Education (Music Education and Student Teaching Coordinator) Job Posting Number 2027045APF Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Fine Arts and Communication Department/School School of Music Position Description The School of Music at Texas State University seeks an engaging, creative, collaborative, and dedicated educator to serve as a non-tenure-track, assistant professor of instruction of Music Education (Student Teaching Coordinator). The successful candidate will provide leadership in two primary areas: music education and coordination of the music student teaching program. The position is designed as a balanced assignment (50% administrative/50% instructional) that supports both the preparation of future music educators and the successful administration and supervision of student teaching experiences across all specialization areas. The successful candidate will be expected to: Coordinate the music student/clinical teaching program, including managing student/clinical teaching placements, communicating with the College of Education, collaborating with cooperating teachers and university supervisors, organizing seminars, and overseeing program policies, procedures, and assessment processes. Teach undergraduate courses in music education in area of specialization (courses may include Marching Band Techniques, Instrumental Performance Literature, Instrumental Arranging, Music Teaching in various Classroom Contexts, or Foundations of Music Education). Supervise and mentor student/clinical teachers in field placements. Participate in recruitment, retention, accreditation, and assessment efforts within the Music Education area and the School of Music. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Director of the School of Music. The university seeks candidates whose professional backgrounds include strong organizational skills, a history of effective communication, dedication to an effective team, and a willingness to be part of a university community. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Music Education or a closely related field. Minimum of three years of successful EC-12 teaching experience. Demonstrated expertise in music education and music program organization. Demonstrated organizational and interpersonal skills necessary to work effectively with student/clinical teachers, the College of Education, and cooperating teachers. Experience working effectively and collaboratively with a variety of individuals. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate in Music Education or a closely related field. Experience teaching instrumental music education courses at the collegiate level. Experience coordinating, supervising, or mentoring student/clinical teachers, interns, or early-career music educators. Experience leading student/clinical teaching seminars or overseeing field-based teacher preparation experiences. Demonstrated excellence in music program organization and development. Proven record of mentorship and supervision of university music education students. Proven record of program management and/or organization at the collegiate level or equivalency. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58563 . For full consideration, please submit the following items by October 28, 2026 : Cover Letter. Curriculum Vitae. Contact information (mailing address, phone number, and email address) for three references. A one-page statement presenting your teaching philosophy including, but not limited to, the themes of music teacher preparation, field experiences, and classroom culture. Unofficial transcripts of the last degree earned or in progress (all in one document). The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts for all earned university degrees. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date August 16, 2027 Posting Date 09/29/2026 Review Date 10/28/2026 Close Date 10/28/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58563 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * At time of appointment: will you have a Master\u2019s degree in music education or related field? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58686": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Urban and Regional Planning", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in Urban and Regional Planning Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor in Urban and Regional Planning Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Urban and Regional Planning Job Posting Number 2027021TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Department of Geography and Environmental Studies Position Description The Department of Geography and Environmental Studies at Texas State University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position in Urban and Regional Planning to begin Fall 2027. We seek an urban geographer or planner whose research will expand and complement the department\u2019s existing strengths in urban and regional planning, applied environmental geography, and GIScience. Areas of specialization are open, but may include urban infrastructure systems, planning and public policy, comparative urbanization, housing and finance, or related areas. The successful candidate will be expected to establish an active, externally visible research program; seek external research support; publish in high-quality scholarly outlets; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in urban geography and related areas; mentor undergraduate and graduate students; and contribute service to the department, university, discipline, and broader community. Required Qualifications A Ph.D. degree in geography, urban and regional planning, or urban studies by time of appointment. A demonstrated record of peer-reviewed scholarship. Demonstrated or potential ability to develop a strong research agenda. Demonstrated or potential ability to teach urban geography courses at undergraduate and graduate levels. Preferred Qualifications Applied research interests in urban planning, urban infrastructure management, comparative urbanization, or housing and finance. Demonstrated record of securing external research funding. Demonstrated ability to advise graduate students in urban geography or urban planning. Application Procedures To be considered in the initial pool of candidates, complete applications must be received no later than November 22, 2026 . Complete applications received after this date will only be considered if no viable candidates are identified and hired from the initial pool. This position will remain open until filled. All positions are subject to availability of funds. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58560 . A complete application must include the materials listed below: A letter of application outlining the applicant\u2019s research credentials, plan for extramural funding, teaching experience, and career goals that meets the required and preferred qualifications as stated above. An up-to-date curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). One sample of published scholarship. Reports of teaching evaluations (if available). Names and contact information for three reference letters. References will be contacted for applicants that advance past the initial application review. For inquiries, please email Dr. Eric Sarmiento, chair of the Search Committee, at sarmiento@txstate.edu. Please indicate \u201cUrban and Regional Planning Position\u201d in the subject line of all correspondence. The Department of Geography at Texas State University ( https://www.geo.txstate.edu/ ) has 36 full-time faculty members, around 500 undergraduate majors in BA and BS programs and over 130 graduate students in our Master of Science (MS), Master of Applied Geography ( MAG ), and PhD programs in geography, geographic education, and geographic information science. The Department of Geography is part of the College of Liberal Arts. To learn more about the department, please visit: https://www.geo.txstate.edu . Texas State University is located in San Marcos, a city of about 75,000 residents situated in the beautiful Central Texas Hill Country, 30 miles south of Austin and 48 miles north of San Antonio. The Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching classifies Texas State University as a \u201cDoctoral University: Higher Research Activity,\u201d the second-highest designation for research institutions in the United States. Texas State University is located in the burgeoning Austin-San Antonio corridor, and with ~44,000 students, is among the largest universities in the state. With a diverse campus community including 50% of the student body from ethnic minorities, Texas State University is one of the top 13 producers of Hispanic baccalaureate graduates in the nation. Additional information about Texas State University and its nationally recognized academic programs is available at www.txstate.edu . Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 09/29/2026 Review Date 11/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58560 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Examples of Recent Publications Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have a Ph.D. degree in geography, urban and regional planning, or urban studies by time of appointment? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58685": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor Job Posting Number 2027020TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Political Science Position Description The Department of Political Science at Texas State University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of assistant professor to teach required and elective undergraduate and graduate (MA) courses. The department awards the Bachelor\u2019s Degree and Master of Arts Degree. Required Qualifications Earned PhD in political science by May 2027. Demonstrated potential for exceptional scholarly research and publication focusing on international law and/or international political economy with a focus on trade issues. Ability to teach introductory international relations courses as well as advanced courses in international law or international political economy with a focus on trade issues. Preferred Qualifications Ability to teach courses on East Asian politics from a Comparative Politics perspective. Demonstrated potential for exceptional teaching in relevant areas. Evidence of effective communication and/or collaborative skills. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58515 . A complete application must include the materials listed below: A letter of interest. A current CV. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Evidence of teaching excellence (e.g., syllabi, student evaluations of teaching). A statement of teaching philosophy. One sample of scholarly work (limited to 50 pages double spaced). Three letters of recommendation. To ensure consideration of your application by the search committee, please submit your application by October 15, 2026 . Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. Proposed Start Date August 16, 2027 Posting Date 09/29/2026 Review Date 10/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58515 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Samples of Scholarly Work/Research Evidence of Teaching Experience/Evaluations Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 Letter of Recommendation #3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in political science or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have a Ph.D. in political science. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58624": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Construction Management", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in Construction Management Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor in Construction Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Construction Management Job Posting Number 2027019TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Department of Engineering Technology Position Description The Department of Engineering Technology at Texas State University is seeking applicants to fill a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in our growing Construction Science and Management program, beginning in Fall 2027. The undergraduate program is accredited by the American Council for Construction Education ( ACCE ) and currently serves almost 900 students. The department also operates MS and PhD programs in construction management with in-person and online options. The selected candidate will be expected to excel in teaching and have excellent oral and written English communication skills. The individual selected for this position will be expected to teach at primarily at the undergraduate level, but some graduate courses could be assigned periodically, as departmental needs require. The selected candidate is also expected to conduct research and to secure external funding, establish an independent research program and publish in the areas of building science and construction management, for an emerging research institution. The candidate will also be expected to engage both undergraduate and graduate students in their research activities and to supervise graduate students. In addition, the selected candidate will participate in appropriate service activities at the program, department, university and professional levels. Required Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a closely related field. Undergraduate degree in Construction Management from an ACCE or ABET accredited institution, or in Construction Engineering or Civil Engineering from an ABET accredited institution, or a closely related field from a similarly accredited institution. Excellent oral and written English language skills. Preferred Qualifications Publication record in academic journals and proceedings. The potential for a viable externally funded research program. Three or more years of full-time work experience in a construction management or construction engineering discipline. Research and teaching expertise in one or more of the following areas: Fundamentals of concrete construction, means and methods. Construction equipment and methods. Construction contracts, risk and ethics. Earned construction industry certifications (i.e. Certified Professional Constructor ( CPC ), Project Management Professional ( PMP ), Certified Construction Manager ( CCM ), LEED -AP, DBIA Design-Build Professional, or related). Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58371 . To be considered for the position, applicants are required to submit the following application materials: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Research Statement. Teaching statement (maximum two pages of text, not including supporting materials such as sample class activities, observation letters, or evaluations). Three reference letters, (at least) one of which explicitly addressing teaching. To ensure full consideration, all materials listed above should arrive by November 15, 2026 . Please clearly address how you meet all criteria in your application materials. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 09/25/2026 Review Date 11/16/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58371 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a doctoral degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a closely related field? Yes, I have a doctoral degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a closely related field. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58598": {"title": "Open Rank in Construction Management", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Open Rank in Construction Management Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Open Rank in Construction Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Open Rank in Construction Management Job Posting Number 2027014TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Department of Engineering Technology Position Description The Department of Engineering Technology invites applications for a tenure track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in Construction Management. This position is designed for individuals whose primary focus is on research, scholarly, and creative activities that enhance the research mission of the university, with a strong emphasis on mentoring and supervising PhD students. The successful candidate will play a critical role in supporting doctoral student progression, including dissertation development, research design, and publication. The position carries expectations for actively mentoring doctoral students in their own research throughout their academic journey; conducting externally funded research producing high-impact scholarly work; and teaching graduate level courses. Responsibilities: Mentor and supervise PhD students, including dissertation advising and research development. Contribute to the growth and structure of the PhD program in Construction Management. Support doctoral students through key milestones, including proposal development, research execution, and publication. Develop and sustain an independent, externally funded research program. Lead and manage research teams that include graduate and doctoral students. Publish in high-impact, peer-reviewed journals. Collaborate with faculty, industry, and external research partners. Required Qualifications For all ranks: Earned doctoral degree in construction management, construction engineering, civil engineering, or a closely related field. Demonstrated research competence and scholarly contributions. Evidence of research productivity, including peer-reviewed publications. Demonstrated ability or strong potential to mentor graduate and PhD students. Excellent Oral and Written English Language skills. For Associate Professor: Minimum of five years of independent, externally funded research experience. Demonstrated record of sustained scholarly contributions. Experience mentoring graduate or doctoral students. For Professor: Minimum of ten years of independent, externally funded research experience. Demonstrated national or international recognition in the field. Significant experience mentoring PhD students and supervising dissertation work. Record of leadership in research programs and professional organizations. Preferred Qualifications Experience graduating doctoral students or serving on dissertation committees. Established record of securing external funding. Experience leading interdisciplinary or industry-sponsored research. Alignment with Construction Management research areas such as risk analysis, project delivery, financial controls, operations, or decision-making. Teaching and mentoring students in an online environment. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57911 . To be considered for the position, applicants are required to submit the following application materials: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Research Statement. Teaching Philosophy Three reference letters (at least), one of which explicitly addressing teaching. To ensure full consideration, all materials listed above should arrive by November 15, 2026. Please clearly address how you meet all criteria in your application materials. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 11/16/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57911 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a doctoral degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a closely related field? Yes, I have a doctoral degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a closely related field. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. * Please select the rank you are applying for. Associate Professor Professor Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58592": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Department of Computer Science", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Department of Computer Science Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Department of Computer Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Department of Computer Science Job Posting Number 2027042APF Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Science and Engineering Department/School Computer Science Position Description The Department of Computer Science seeks to develop a pool of candidates for postdoctoral scholars (post-doc) positions in Computer Science. A post-doc is a professional appointment designed to provide recent doctoral degree recipients with an opportunity to gain experiences and skills that will advance their careers. A post-doc works under the supervision and sponsorship of a regular faculty member, who serves as a mentor to the post-doc, and it is expected that the faculty sponsor will provide an orientation and development plan for the post-doc, impart the realities and variety of careers available to the post-doc, and encourage learning opportunities to broaden the post-doc\u2019s aspirations and experiences. The appointment involves substantial and full-time commitment to research, scholarship, teaching, or other professional activities. Eligibility for annual reappointment is contingent upon satisfactory annual performance evaluations during the term period, in addition to continuity of funding and departmental/school need. Required Qualifications Recently awarded a Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications Excellent verbal and written communication skills Demonstrated ability to conduct research independently and in groups Previous teaching experience is preferred. Application Procedures The Department of Computer Science will accept applications from qualified applicants on a continual basis. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University site will be considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58463 . Interested individuals should submit the following: Current CV. Cover Letter/Letter of interest outlining specific academic and professional experiences relevant for a postdoc research appointment. Statement of research interests. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for two (2) academic references who can provide information about the applicant\u2019s research skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from the highest degree-granting institution. Type of Position Full-Time Proposed Start Date 10/01/2026 Posting Date 09/22/2026 Review Date 09/30/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58463 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctorate in Computer Science or a closely related field? Yes, I have a doctorate in computer science or closely related field No, I do not * How many years of teaching experience do you have at the university level? No prior teaching experience. Less than 1 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years or more * Describe your prior teaching experience (if any) including experience teaching classes that are delivered face-to-face, online, or remotely. Include a list of all classes taught. (Open Ended Question) * Which semester(s) do you wish to be considered for? Fall, Spring, Summer or Combination? (Open Ended Question) * What is your schedule availability? Days/Nights; Days of the Week; Location (e.g., San Marcos, Round Rock, online courses, etc.) (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58582": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Physical Geography", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in Physical Geography Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor in Physical Geography Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Physical Geography Job Posting Number 2027018TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Department of Geography and Environmental Studies Position Description The Department of Geography and Environmental Studies at Texas State University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position in Physical Geography with a specialization in climatology to begin Fall 2027. We are particularly interested in candidates whose scholarship focuses on climatic processes at a range of spatial and temporal scales and their interactions with the Earth\u2019s spheres and environmental systems. We seek a scholar whose research will complement the department\u2019s existing strengths in water resources, geomorphology, environmental hazards and disasters, energy resources, community resilience, and human\u2013environment interactions. The successful candidate will be expected to establish an active, externally visible research program; seek external research support; publish in scholarly outlets; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in climatology and related areas in the candidate\u2019s area of expertise; mentor undergraduate and graduate students; and contribute service to the department, university, discipline, and broader community. Texas State University is located in San Marcos, a city of about 75,000 residents situated in the beautiful Central Texas Hill Country, 30 miles south of Austin and 48 miles north of San Antonio. The Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching classifies Texas State University as a \u201cDoctoral University: Higher Research Activity,\u201d the second-highest designation for research institutions in the United States. Texas State University is located in the burgeoning Austin-San Antonio corridor, and with ~44,000 students, is among the largest universities in the state. With a diverse campus community including 50% of the student body from ethnic minorities, Texas State University is one of the top 13 producers of Hispanic baccalaureate graduates in the nation. Additional information about Texas State University and its nationally recognized academic programs is available at www.txstate.edu . Required Qualifications Ph.D. degree in Geography or a related field, with a specialization in climatology, by time of appointment. Demonstrated record of peer-reviewed scholarship in climatology, oceanography, and/or environmental systems research. Demonstrated or potential ability to develop a strong research agenda. Demonstrated or potential ability to teach climatology, meteorology, oceanography, quantitative methods, or related environmental systems courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated record of research that applies climatology to complex environmental challenges. Demonstrated record of using research methods such as field methods, quantitative methods, advanced modeling, or GIScience and remote sensing. Demonstrated or potential ability securing external research funding. Demonstrated or potential ability to advise graduate students. Application Procedures To be considered in the initial pool of candidates, complete applications must be received no later than November 22, 2026 . Complete applications received after this date will only be considered if no viable candidates are identified and hired from the initial pool. This position will remain open until filled. All positions are subject to availability of funds. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58559 . A complete application must include the materials listed below: A letter of application outlining the applicant\u2019s research credentials, plan for extramural funding, teaching experience, and career goals that meets the required and preferred qualifications as stated above. An up-to-date curriculum vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). One sample of published scholarship. Reports of teaching evaluations (if available). Names and contact information for three reference letters. References will be contacted for applicants that advance past the initial application review. For inquiries, please email Dr. Ed Chow, chair of the Search Committee, at chow@txstate.edu. Please indicate \u201cPhysical Geography Position\u201d in the subject line of all correspondence. The Department of Geography at Texas State University ( https://www.geo.txstate.edu/ ) has 36 full-time faculty members, around 500 undergraduate majors in BA and BS programs and over 130 graduate students in our Master of Science (MS), Master of Applied Geography ( MAG ), and PhD programs in geography, geographic education, and geographic information science. The Department of Geography is part of the College of Liberal Arts. To learn more about the department, please visit: https://www.geo.txstate.edu . Proposed Start Date 8/16/2027 Posting Date 09/22/2026 Review Date 11/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58559 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Examples of Recent Publications Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Will you have a Ph.D. in Geography or a related field with a specialization in climatology by the time of appointment? Yes No Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58543": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Technical Communication", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Technical Communication Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor, Technical Communication Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor, Technical Communication Job Posting Number 2027005TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department English Position Description The Department of English at Texas State University invites applicants for a full-time (nine-month) tenure-track faculty position at the rank of assistant professor to begin in Fall 2027 at our San Marcos campus. The successful candidate will be expected to sustain a significant, ongoing research agenda leading to peer-reviewed publication in the field of technical communication. The candidate will also teach in the M.A. in Technical Communication Program and in our growing undergraduate technical communication offerings. Additional duties include significant participation in, and contributions to the continued development of, graduate and undergraduate programs in technical communication. The typical teaching load for assistant professors in their first two years is 2/2. In the third year and beyond, the typical teaching load is 3/3 with some opportunities for course load reduction. Course offerings typically include a mixture of face-to-face, hybrid, and online modalities. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in technical communication or closely related field, with degree completed at time of appointment. Strong, ongoing record of productive scholarship, evidenced by peer-reviewed publications in technical communication journals and/or book series. Expertise sufficient to direct master\u2019s theses and/or doctoral dissertations in technical communication. Preferred Qualifications Industry experience as a technical writer, information architect, UX designer/researcher, content strategist, or related position. Research and teaching specialties in areas that widen Texas State University\u2019s current and proposed graduate program curricula including, but not limited to, digital humanities, emerging technologies, international technical communication, and professional. communication related to the fields of criminal justice, construction science, and engineering Ability to teach varied curriculum in technical communication, including courses such as editing, science writing, structured authoring, international technical communication, content management, data visualization, UX research with AI, writing with AI, and document design. Evidence of experience developing and submitting competitive research grant applications, accompanied by an explanation of the impact of awarded funds, if any, on the candidate\u2019s research agenda.. Experience teaching in online or hybrid modalities. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58159 . For full consideration, please submit the following by September 21, 2026 : Cover letter addressing qualifications. Curriculum Vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). Research agenda (1-2 pages). Teaching philosophy (1-2 pages). Contact information for three references. Questions regarding this position should be directed to Dr. Chris Dayley, Search Committee Chair, at chris.dayley@txstate.edu Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 08/26/2026 Review Date 10/21/2026 Close Date 10/21/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58159 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) List of References Statement of Teaching Philosophy Comprehensive Research Agenda Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a Ph.D. in technical communication or closely related field, with your degree completed at time of appointment? Yes, I have a Ph.D. in technical communication or closely related field, with degree completed at time of appointment No, I do not/will not have a Ph.D. in technical communication or closely related field, with degree completed at time of appointment Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58531": {"title": "Open Rank in Sport Management", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Open Rank in Sport Management Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Open Rank in Sport Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Open Rank in Sport Management Job Posting Number 2027017TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Dept of Health & Human Performance Position Description The Department of Health and Human Performance at Texas State University invites applications for a tenure-track Professor in Sport Management beginning Fall 2027. A primary responsibility of this position is to support the Department\u2019s newly developed hybrid Ph.D. in Kinesiology with a concentration in Sport Management. The doctoral program prepares graduates for careers in higher education, research, and leadership within the sport and health studies industries. Faculty in the program are expected to maintain productive research programs and provide active mentorship for doctoral students, including dissertation supervision and participation on doctoral committees. This program is launching an Exercise Science concentration Fall 2026 (hybrid: online and face-to-face courses), and a Sport Management (online courses) concentration Fall 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued development and delivery of the doctoral program through teaching doctoral courses, mentoring doctoral students, supervising dissertations, and maintaining a sustained program of scholarly research. This candidate may also teach classes in other programs in HHP such as Recreation and Sport Management. Texas State is pursuing Carnegie R1 classification, and the department seeks candidates with a strong commitment to and potential for high-impact scholarly productivity, external funding development, and doctoral student mentorship. The successful candidate will contribute to a collaborative research environment and support scholarship related to sport management and the sport industry. University: Founded in 1899, Texas State University is a doctoral-granting institution with more than 38,000 students. The university holds a Carnegie classification of Doctoral University \u2013 High Research Activity (R2) and is implementing a strategic plan to achieve Doctoral University \u2013 Very High Research Activity (R1) status. Texas State is located in San Marcos along the San Marcos River within the rapidly growing corridor between Austin and San Antonio. Department: The Department of Health and Human Performance includes more than 40 full-time faculty members and serves approximately 2,500 undergraduate and graduate students across programs in Athletic Training, Exercise and Sports Science, Public Health, and Recreation and Sport Management. Faculty maintain active research agendas and contribute to collaborative scholarship across multiple areas of human performance and sport. Responsibilities: Support the Ph.D. in Kinesiology program, particularly the Sport Management concentration (launching fall 2027) Teach doctoral, master\u2019s, and undergraduate courses in the Recreation and Sport Management division. Serve as an advisor for graduate research including doctoral dissertations. Maintain a sustained program of scholarly research resulting in peer-reviewed publications. Pursue externally funded research and contribute to collaborative grant initiatives where appropriate. Contribute to the department\u2019s research productivity and national visibility. Participate in departmental, college, and university service. Maintain active engagement with professional organizations and the sport industry. Required Qualifications Assistant Professor: Earned doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DBA , or equivalent) in Sport Management, Sport Administration, Sport Business, Kinesiology with a sport management emphasis, or a closely related field by the time of appointment Evidence of an emerging program of scholarly research related to sport management or the sport industry Evidence of potential for sustained research and scholarship Evidence of potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring graduate students Associate Professor: Earned doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DBA , or equivalent) in Sport Management, Sport Administration, Sport Business, Kinesiology with a sport management emphasis, or a closely related field. Eligible for tenure at the Associate Professor rank at time of hire. Evidence of an established and productive research agenda related to sport management or the sport industry. Evidence of effectiveness in teaching and mentoring graduate students. Professor: Earned doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DBA , or equivalent) in Sport Management, Sport Administration, Sport Business, Kinesiology with a sport management emphasis, or a closely related field. Eligible for tenure at the Professor rank at time of hire. Evidence of a sustained scholarly research agenda related to sport management or the sport industry. Evidence of excellence in teaching and mentoring graduate students. Preferred Qualifications Assistant Professor: Evidence of an active and productive research agenda in sport management. Evidence of external funding activity or potential for securing external research support. Experience teaching sport management courses at the graduate or doctoral level. Evidence of excellence in teaching using various instructional modes, including online. Experience mentoring graduate students or serving on thesis/dissertation committees. Evidence of collaborative research and interdisciplinary scholarship. Evidence of engagement with professional organizations related to sport management. Prior experience at the assistant professor rank. Associate Professor: Evidence of external funding activity or potential for securing external research support. Experience mentoring graduate students or serving on thesis/dissertation committees. Evidence of collaborative research and interdisciplinary scholarship. Experience teaching sport management courses at the graduate or doctoral level. Evidence of effectiveness in teaching using various instructional modes, including online. Evidence of engagement with professional organizations related to sport management. Evidence of scholarly or applied expertise in sport marketing, consumer behavior, sport analytics, or other specialized areas related to sport management. Prior experience as an academic program coordinator or program director. Professor: Evidence of external funding activity and securing external research support. Experience mentoring graduate students or serving on thesis/dissertation committees. Evidence of collaborative research and interdisciplinary scholarship. Experience teaching sport management courses at the graduate or doctoral level. Evidence of effectiveness in teaching using various instructional modes, including online. Evidence of engagement with professional organizations related to sport management. Evidence of scholarly or applied expertise in sport marketing, consumer behavior, sport analytics, or other specialized areas related to sport management. Prior experience as an academic program coordinator or program director. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University employment website will be accepted: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58478 . Applicants should submit: Letter of application addressing the required qualifications (cover letter). Curriculum vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (combined into a single document). Contact information for three professional references. Two representative scholarly publications and/or works in progress. Proposed Start Date 8/16/2027 Posting Date 09/18/2026 Review Date 11/11/2026 Close Date 11/09/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58478 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) List of References Examples of Recent Publications Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DBA, or equivalent) in Sport Management, Sport Administration, Sport Business, Kinesiology with a sport management emphasis, or a closely related field by the time of appointment? Yes, I have an earned doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DBA, or equivalent) in Sport Management, Sport Administration, Sport Business, Kinesiology with a sport management emphasis, or a closely related field. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion by the time of appointment. No, I do not have an earned doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DBA, or equivalent) in Sport Management, Sport Administration, Sport Business, Kinesiology with a sport management emphasis, or a closely related field. * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Professor Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58483": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Professional Counseling", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Professional Counseling Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Professional Counseling Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Professional Counseling Job Posting Number 2027016TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Conslng, Ldrship, Adlt Educ & Schl Psych Position Description The Department of Counseling, Leadership, Adult Education, and School Psychology ( CLAS ) in the College of Education at Texas State University, a Hispanic-Serving Institution ( HSI ) located in San Marcos, Texas, invites applications for a tenure-earning assistant professor position of Professional Counseling beginning August 2027. This position is focused on teaching and research in the School Counseling Concentration and involves teaching, research, service, and program support in a vibrant master\u2019s program in Central Texas. Specific responsibilities include teaching courses in Professional Counseling, maintaining an active and productive program of research, engaging in external funding submissions, and providing service to the program, department, university, and profession. Program: The Professional Counseling Program is CACREP -accredited in three specialty areas: Clinical Mental Health Counseling; Marriage, Couple, and Family Counseling; and School Counseling. This position will include teaching core courses in our counseling program, with a particular focus on school counseling courses, Developmental Issues, and Child and Adolescent Counseling. The successful candidate will be headquartered on the main university campus in San Marcos and will teach courses on both the main university campus in San Marcos and at the university\u2019s Round Rock campus. Department: The CLAS Department serves approximately 975 students seeking undergraduate, master\u2019s, and doctoral degrees in Professional Counseling ( COUN ), Educational and Community Leadership ( EDCL ), Adult, Professional, and Community Education ( APCE ), School Psychology ( SPSY ), Student Affairs in Higher Education ( SAHE ), and Integrated Studies ( INTS ). The CLAS Department provides high quality undergraduate and graduate education to promote significant transformational changes in communities, schools, organizations, and institutions locally and globally. Guided by expert faculty who are deeply engaged in innovative research and dedicated to student success, CLAS students grow into leaders and changemakers in schools, communities, and organizations across Texas and beyond. The CLAS Department is proud to be part of a public, Hispanic-Serving Institution that values discovery and impact through research, teaching, and service. University: Founded in 1899 as a small teaching college, Texas State University is now home to over 40,000 students. The university holds a Carnegie classification of Doctoral University-High Research Activity (R2) and is engaged in a strategic plan to attain Doctoral University-Very High Research Activity (R1) by 2027. Texas State University is located along the beautiful San Marcos River. San Marcos is in the center of the innovation corridor, 40 minutes south of Austin and 60 minutes north of San Antonio and is rich in vibrant and eclectic communities. Required Qualifications An earned doctorate in Counselor Education by employment date of August 2027. A demonstrated record of training and experience in school counseling. A record of, or demonstration of the potential for, research and publication at the national and/or international levels. A record of, or demonstration of the potential for, securing external funding for research. A professional clinical license (e.g., Licensed Professional Counselor [ LPC ], Licensed Marriage and Family Therapist [ LMFT ]) or School Counselor certification or a provisional clinical license (e.g., LPC Associate, LMFT Associate) with a plan in place to complete the professional license in the State of Texas within two years. Preferred Qualifications A documented record of securing external funding for research. Experience teaching core courses in a CACREP -accredited program in the teaching areas listed above. Designation as a clinical supervisor (e.g., LPC -S, LMFT -S) and experience providing clinical supervision in an academic and/or clinical setting. A professional certification in play therapy (e.g., Registered Play Therapist [RPT\u2122], Registered Play Therapist Supervisor [ RPT -S\u2122], School- Based Registered Play Therapist [SB-RPT\u2122]). A demonstrated record of training and experience in play therapy. Application Procedures Only applications submitted for this specific posting through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58376 . To guarantee full consideration, all application materials must be submitted by October 14, 2026 . Applicants must submit: A letter of interest that specifically addresses the qualifications and responsibilities noted in this posting. Current curriculum vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). Names and contact information (to include phone and email address) of five references. Three reprints of recent publications (optional). Inquiries about this position may be directed to Dr. Jennifer Greene-Rooks, Search Committee Chair, jgreene@txstate.edu. The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting institutions. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 10/15/2026 Close Date 10/27/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58376 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) List of References Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Licensure Certifications Letter of Recommendation #2 Examples of Recent Publications Examples of Recent Publications #2 Examples of Recent Publications #3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned doctorate in counselor education from a CACREP-accredited program or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have an earned doctorate in counselor education from a CACREP-accredited program. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58482": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Educational and Community Leadership", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Educational and Community Leadership Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Educational and Community Leadership Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Educational and Community Leadership Job Posting Number 2027015TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Conslng, Ldrship, Adlt Educ & Schl Psych Position Description The Department of Counseling, Leadership, Adult Education, and School Psychology ( CLAS ) in the College of Education at Texas State University, a Hispanic-Serving Institution ( HSI ) located in San Marcos, Texas, invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Educational and Community Leadership beginning August 2027. This position involves teaching, research, service, and leadership in our vibrant master\u2019s and doctoral programs in Central Texas. Position: This position involves teaching, research, and service. Specific responsibilities include: Teaching graduate courses in the Ph.D. and the master\u2019s degree programs in Educational and Community Leadership, and the Principal and Superintendent Certification Programs. Teaching and service will be required across these programs in multiple locations, including on the main campus in San Marcos, supporting the growing expansion of our programs on the Round Rock Campus, and in partnership cohort programs in surrounding school districts. Developing and maintaining an active and productive research agenda that results in peer-reviewed publications and national and international visibility; commensurate with the university and department expectations for tenure and/or promotion. Seeking or having the potential to seek external funding to support research and student development. Contributing to service activities at the program, department, college, and university level, and the broader educational leadership profession. Mentoring master\u2019s and doctoral students; the latter through the dissertation process to timely degree completion. For additional information about the Department of Counseling, Leadership, Adult Education, and School Psychology please visit: https://www.txst.edu/clas.html Program: The Educational and Community Leadership ( EDCL ) program prepares leaders in K\u201312 and community-based contexts. The program emphasizes leadership, research-informed practice, and quality educational experience. Department: The CLAS Department serves approximately 975 students seeking undergraduate, master\u2019s, and doctoral degrees in Professional Counseling ( COUN ), Educational and Community Leadership ( EDCL ), Adult, Professional, and Community Education ( APCE ), School Psychology ( SPSY ), Student Affairs in Higher Education ( SAHE ), and Integrated Studies ( INTS ). The CLAS Department provides high quality undergraduate and graduate education to promote significant transformational changes in communities, schools, organizations, and institutions locally and globally. Guided by expert faculty who are deeply engaged in innovative research and dedicated to student success, CLAS students grow into leaders and changemakers in schools, communities, and organizations across Texas and beyond. The CLAS Department is proud to be part of a public, Hispanic-Serving Institution that values discovery and impact through research, teaching, and service. University: Founded in 1899 as a small teaching college, Texas State University is now home to over 40,000 students. The university holds a Carnegie classification of Doctoral University-High Research Activity (R2) and is engaged in a strategic plan to attain Doctoral University-Very High Research Activity (R1) by 2027. Texas State University is located along the beautiful San Marcos River. San Marcos is in the center of the innovation corridor, 40 minutes south of downtown Austin and 60 minutes north of San Antonio and is rich in vibrant and eclectic communities. Required Qualifications Required qualifications for Assistant Professor rank: An earned doctorate in Educational Leadership, Educational Administration, or closely related field. Experience in educational leadership preparation and/or prior leadership roles in K\u201312 settings (e.g., assistant principal, principal, district administrator). Record of, or demonstration of the potential for, sustained research and publication in peer-reviewed journals and at the national and/or international levels. Record of, or demonstration of the potential for, securing external funding for research. Record of, or demonstration of the potential for, excellence in graduate-level teaching, including experience teaching doctoral-level courses. Record of, or demonstration of the potential for, mentoring and supervising doctoral students through to completion of their dissertation and degree. Record of, or demonstration of the potential for, service and academic leadership at the program, department, college, and professional levels. Preferred Qualifications Preferred qualifications for Assistant Professor rank: Experience as a K\u201312 school or district leader at the level of principal or higher. Experience teaching courses in an Educational Leadership or Educational Administration program. Experience supervising and mentoring doctoral students through dissertation completion. Demonstrated success in building and sustaining district and community partnerships. Application Procedures Only applications submitted for this specific posting through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58377 . To guarantee full consideration, all application materials must be submitted by October 14, 2026 . To apply, submit: A letter of interest that specifically addresses the qualifications and responsibilities noted in this posting. Current curriculum vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). Names and contact information (to include phone and email address) of three references Three reprints of recent publications (optional). Inquiries about this position may be directed to Dr. Rolf Straubhaar, Search Committee Chair, at straubhaar@txstate.edu The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting institutions. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 10/15/2026 Close Date 10/27/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58377 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) List of References Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Letter of Recommendation #1 Letter of Recommendation #2 Examples of Recent Publications Examples of Recent Publications #2 Examples of Recent Publications #3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned PhD in Educational Leadership, Educational Administration, or closely related field? Yes, I have a PhD in Educational Leadership, Educational Administration, or a related field No, I do not Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58462": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Ingram School of Engineering", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Ingram School of Engineering Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Ingram School of Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Ingram School of Engineering Job Posting Number 2027040NTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Science and Engineering Department/School Ingram School of Engineering Position Description The Ingram School of Engineering seeks to develop a pool of candidates for postdoctoral scholar (post-doc) positions in Civil Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Industrial Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, and Mechanical Engineering. For information about the various areas visit the Ingram School of Engineering . A post-doc is a professional appointment designed to provide recent doctoral degree recipients with an opportunity to gain experiences and skills that will advance their careers. A post-doc works under the supervision and sponsorship of a regular faculty member, who serves as a mentor to the post-doc, and it is expected that the faculty sponsor will provide an orientation and development plan for the post-doc, impart the realities and variety of careers available to the post-doc, and encourage learning opportunities to broaden the post-doc\u2019s aspirations and experiences. The appointment involves substantial and full-time commitment to research, scholarship, teaching, or other professional activities. Eligibility for annual reappointment is contingent upon satisfactory annual performance evaluations during the term period, in addition to continuity of funding and departmental/school need. For more information, please visit Postdoctoral Scholar Appointments, AA/ PPS No. 04.01.24 (7.21) . This posting is for September 2026 \u2013 August 2027 hires. Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool faculty position will be available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. Required Qualifications Recently awarded a Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate (e.g., D.Sc.., M.D.). Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience is preferred. Application Procedures The Ingram School of Engineering will accept applications from qualified applicants on a continual basis. Applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58361 . Interested individuals should submit: A current CV Letter of interest outlining specific academic and professional experiences relevant for a postdoc research appointment. A statement of research interests Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide information about the applicant\u2019s research skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from the highest degree granting institution. Type of Position Temporary Full-Time or Part-Time Proposed Start Date FY2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 05/31/2027 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58361 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Research Interests Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Samples of Scholarly Work/Research Examples of Recent Publications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have you been awarded a Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate? (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate the specific program area(s) for which you wish to be considered: Civil Engineering Electrical Engineering Industrial Engineering Manufacturing Engineering Mechanical Engineering * What is your schedule availability? Days/Nights; Days of the Week; Location (e.g., San Marcos, Round Rock, online courses, etc.) (Open Ended Question) * How many years of teaching experience do you have at the university level? No prior teaching experience. Less than 1 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years or more * Describe your prior teaching experience (if any) including experience teaching classes that are delivered face-to-face, online, or remotely. Include a list of all classes taught. (Open Ended Question) * Which semester(s) do you wish to be considered for? Fall, Spring, Summer or Combination? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58461": {"title": "Nontenure Faculty Pool-Department of Chemistry &amp; Biochemistry", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Nontenure Faculty Pool-Department of Chemistry &amp; Biochemistry Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Nontenure Faculty Pool-Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Nontenure Faculty Pool-Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry Job Posting Number 2027039NTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Science and Engineering Department/School Chemistry and Biochemistry Position Description The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry seeks to develop a pool of candidates for possible temporary/nontenured faculty to teach. Temporary/nontenured faculty are appointed to teach one to four courses per semester. Teaching appointments are based upon student demand on a semester-by-semester basis. Eligibility for annual reappointment is contingent upon satisfactory annual performance evaluations during the term period, in addition to continuity of funding and departmental/school need. Successful candidates will teach at the Texas State University campus in San Marcos, Texas. This posting is for the Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027 semesters. Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool faculty position will be available to the departmental search committee for consideration as the need arises. Required Qualifications A minimum of a master\u2019s degree in Chemistry or Biochemistry. Strong academic background in one or more of the following areas: general chemistry, biochemistry, and organic chemistry. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications A Ph.D. in Chemistry or Biochemistry or a closely related field. Previous experience teaching undergraduate courses as the instructor of record. Previous experience coordinating and developing curriculum for undergraduate laboratories. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58335 . To ensure full consideration please submit the following: Cover Letter. Curriculum Vitae. Letter of Teaching Philosophy. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Questions regarding this position should be addressed to department chair Dr. Soumitra Basu, tcp79@txstate.edu or associate chair, Dr. Wendi David, wd11@txstate.edu . Texas State University, 601 University Drive, San Marcos, TX 78666. Candidates selected for hire will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting universities. Type of Position Temporary Full-Time or Part-Time Proposed Start Date FY 2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 06/30/2027 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58335 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned masters or doctorate in chemistry, biochemistry, or a closely related field or anticipate completion prior to start date? Yes, I have an earned doctorate in chemistry, biochemistry, or a closely related field. Yes, I have an earned masters in chemistry, biochemistry, or a closely related field No * Which location are you interested in teaching at? San Marcos, TX Round Rock, TX Online/Remote No Preference * How many years of teaching experience do you have at the university level? No prior teaching experience. Less than 1 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years or more * Describe your prior teaching experience (if any) including experience teaching classes that are delivered face-to-face, online, or remotely. Include a list of all classes taught. (Open Ended Question) * Which semester(s) do you wish to be considered for? Spring, Summer, or Combination? (Open Ended Question) * What is your schedule availability? Days/Nights; Days of the Week; Location (e.g., San Marcos, Round Rock, online courses, etc.) (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58456": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design Job Posting Number 2027012TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department School of Theatre, Dance, & Film Position Description The School of Theatre, Dance, and Film at Texas State University seeks an Assistant or Associate Professor of Scenic Design (Tenure Track or Professor of Practice), starting fall 2027. The successful candidate will join a nationally recognized department with a dynamic faculty dedicated to a collaborative and immersive approach to teaching graduate and undergraduate students. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Teach graduate and undergraduate courses in scenic design and related topics which may include drafting, history, analysis, and graphic skills. Mentor and advise graduate and undergraduate student designers on realized production work. Actively recruit exceptional candidates for the MFA design program. Participate in department production season planning. Collaborate with the Design, Technology, and Management Area in support of current initiatives and new developments. Maintain an active agenda of creative and/or scholarly research including occasional designs for department productions. Provide service to the School, College, and University, commensurate with rank. Required Qualifications Required qualifications for Assistant Professor Rank (Tenure Line): MFA in Theatre Design. Active record of professional scenic design experience in regional and/or commercial theatre. Strong CAD skills utilizing industry standard (Schematic, 3D, and Visualization). Strong digital and/or hand graphic skills that align with industry standards. Required qualifications for Associate Professor Rank (Tenure Line): MFA in Theatre Design. Extensive and active record of professional scenic design experience in regional and/or commercial theatre; minimum of 7 years to be considered for Associate Rank. Strong CAD skills utilizing industry standard (Schematic, 3D, and Visualization). Strong digital and/or hand graphic skills that align with industry standards. University/college teaching experience. Required qualifications for Assistant Professor of Practice Rank: Bachelor\u2019s degree. Active record of professional scenic design experience in regional and/or commercial theatre; minimum of 7 years. Strong CAD skills utilizing industry standard (Schematic, 3D, and Visualization). Strong digital and/or hand graphic skills that align with industry standards. Required qualifications for Associate Professor of Practice Rank: Bachelor\u2019s degree. Extensive and active record of professional scenic design experience in regional and/or commercial theatre; minimum of 12 years. Strong CAD skills utilizing industry standard (Schematic, 3D, and Visualization). Strong digital and/or hand graphic skills that align with industry standards. The successful applicant will receive the appropriate rank and title based on university and school established standards. Preferred Qualifications Experience in a secondary design discipline with a preference for costume or projection design. Experience teaching at the graduate and/or undergraduate level. Demonstrated mentorship of graduate students and/or assistant designers. Proven track record of effective collaboration. Experience in non-theatrical applications of design (e.g., themed environment, events). Demonstrated organizational and leadership skills suitable for academic program oversight. Application Procedures The position will remain open until filled. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58372 . For full consideration, applications should be received by October 18, 2026 . A current CV Cover letter that includes your qualifications and fit with the job description. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 10/18/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58372 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Artistic Philosophy Digital Files (Personal Creative Works) Statement of Teaching/Mentorship Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Portfolio List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a M.F.A. in Theatre with an emphasis in Technical Production or related field by date of hire? Yes, I have a M.F.A. in Theatre with an emphasis in Technical Production or related field. Yes, anticipated completion of the M.F.A. in Theatre with an emphasis in Technical Production or related field prior to start date. No. * Do you have a Bachelor's degree? yes No * Please select the rank you are applying for. Assistant Professor Associate Professor Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58449": {"title": "Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Chemistry &amp; Biochemistry", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Chemistry &amp; Biochemistry Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Chemistry & Biochemistry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Postdoctoral Scholar Pool - Chemistry & Biochemistry Job Posting Number 2027038NTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Science and Engineering Department/School Chemistry and Biochemistry Position Description The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry seeks to develop a pool of candidates for postdoctoral scholars (post-doc) position in Chemistry and Biochemistry. A post-doc is a professional appointment designed to provide recent doctoral degree recipients with an opportunity to gain experiences and skills that will advance their careers. A post-doc works under the supervision and sponsorship of a regular faculty member, who serves as a mentor to the post-doc, and it is expected that the faculty sponsor will provide an orientation and development plan for the post-doc, impart the realities and variety of careers available to the post-doc, and encourage learning opportunities to broaden the post-doc\u2019s aspirations and experiences. The appointment involves substantial and full-time commitment to research, scholarship, teaching, or other professional activities. Eligibility for annual reappointment is contingent upon satisfactory annual performance evaluations during the term period, in addition to continuity of funding and departmental/school need. For more information, please visit Postdoctoral Scholar Appointments, AA/ PPS No. 04.01.24 (7.21) . Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool faculty position will be available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. This position is subject to the availability of funds. Required Qualifications Recently awarded a Ph.D. chemistry, biochemistry, biomedical engineering, biomolecular engineering, chemical engineering, materials science and engineering, polymer science, or a closely related fields. Preferred Qualifications Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated ability to conduct research independently and in groups Experience in preparing scientific publications. Application Procedures The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry will accept applications from qualified applicants on a continual basis. Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58193 . Interested individuals should submit the following: Current CV. Letter of interest outlining specific academic and professional experiences relevant for a postdoc research appointment. Statement of research interests. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide information about the applicant\u2019s research skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from the highest degree-granting institution. Type of Position Temporary Full-Time or Part-Time Proposed Start Date Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 06/30/2027 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58193 Special Instructions Summary Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Licensure Certifications Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold a Ph.D. in chemistry, biochemistry, biomedical engineering, biomolecular engineering, chemical engineering, materials science and engineering, polymer science, or a closely related field? Yes No * What are your research areas? (Open Ended Question) * What is your schedule availability? Days/Nights; Days of the Week; Location (e.g., San Marcos, Round Rock, online courses, etc.) (Open Ended Question) * How many years of teaching experience do you have at the university level? No prior teaching experience. Less than 1 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years or more * Describe your prior teaching experience (if any) including experience teaching classes that are face-to-face, online or remotely. Include a list of all classes taught. (Open Ended Question) * Which semester(s) do you wish to be considered for? Fall, Spring, Summer, or Combination? (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58447": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Shakespeare and Early Modern Literature", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in Shakespeare and Early Modern Literature Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor in Shakespeare and Early Modern Literature Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Shakespeare and Early Modern Literature Job Posting Number 2027009TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department English Position Description The Department of English at Texas State University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, with specialty in Shakespeare and Early Modern Literature and Culture. The successful applicant will maintain an active research agenda and record of publication and will teach both undergraduate and graduate courses on Shakespeare. In addition to Shakespeare, teaching assignments may include courses within candidate\u2019s other areas of interest. Ability to teach and conduct research in one (or more) of the following areas: Seventeenth- and/or Eighteenth-Century British Literature; drama; material culture and performance histories; global Shakespeare and adaptation studies; textual editing; early modern environmental humanities and ecocriticism and/or digital humanities are especially desirable. The teaching assignment may include core English courses, such as introductory literature surveys. All positions are subject to availability of funds. Appointment begins Fall 2027. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in English or closely related field that meets accreditation requirements (18 graduate hours in English), with degree completed at time of appointment. Specialization in Shakespeare and Early Modern Literature and Culture Background and/or experience commensurate with the position of assistant professor and sufficient to teach graduate courses in the specialization. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability in scholarly research on Shakespeare and Early Modern Literature and Culture. Documented Experience teaching Shakespeare at the post-secondary level Ability to teach and conduct research in one (or more) of the following areas: Seventeenth and/or Eighteenth Century British Literature; drama; material culture and performance histories; global Shakespeare and adaptation studies; textual editing; or early modern environmental humanities and ecocriticism and/or digital humanities. Experience in mentoring and advising under-represented students. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58315 . For full consideration, please submit the following by November 1st, 2026: Cover Letter. Curriculum Vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). Sample syllabi. List of References. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Questions regarding this position should be directed to Dr. Victoria Smith, Search Committee Chair, at vlsmith@txstate.edu Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 11/01/2026 Close Date 11/01/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58315 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) List of References Syllabi Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in English or closely related field that meets accreditation requirements, with a minimum of 18 graduate hours in English and degree completed at time of appointment? Yes, I have an earned Ph.D. in English or closely related field that meets accreditation requirements, with a minimum of 18 graduate hours in English. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58446": {"title": "Assistant Professor in American Literature and culture before 1877", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor in American Literature and culture before 1877 Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor in American Literature and culture before 1877 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor in American Literature and culture before 1877 Job Posting Number 2027008TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department English Position Description The Department of English at Texas State University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor, with specialty in American literature and culture before 1877. The successful applicant will maintain an active record of publication and teach both undergraduate and graduate courses in their area of specialization. We are especially interested in scholars whose research and teaching interests fall into one (or more) of the following areas: Indigenous, Latinx, or African American writing in English, conquest and colonialism studies, and/or slave narratives. The teaching assignment may include core English courses, such as introductory literature surveys. All positions are subject to availability of funds. Appointment begins Fall 2027. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in English or closely related field that meets accreditation requirements (18 graduate hours in English), with degree completed at time of appointment. Specialization in American literature and culture before 1877. Demonstrated teaching excellence. Background and/or experience commensurate with the position of assistant professor and sufficient to teach graduate courses in American literature and culture before 1877. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated ability in scholarly research on American literature and culture before 1877. Ability to teach and conduct research in one (or more) of the following areas: Indigenous, Latinx, or African American writing in English, conquest and colonialism studies, and/or slave narratives. Experience in mentoring and advising under-represented students. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58323 . For full consideration, please submit the following by November 1st, 2026: Cover Letter. Curriculum Vitae. Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document). List of References. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Questions regarding this position should be directed to Dr. Robert Tally, Search Committee Chair, at robert.tally@txstate.edu Proposed Start Date 08/16/2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 11/01/2026 Close Date 11/01/2026 Open Until Filled? No Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58323 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) List of References Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in English or closely related field that meets accreditation requirements, with a minimum of 18 graduate hours in English and degree completed at time of appointment? Yes, I have an earned Ph.D. in English or closely related field that meets accreditation requirements, with a minimum of 18 graduate hours in English. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58445": {"title": "Chair, Department of Psychology", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Chair, Department of Psychology Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Chair, Department of Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must be submitted through the Texas State University website. For full consideration, please submit application materials by November 15, 2026 (review of applications begins November 16, 2026). Required Application Documents: \u00b7 Cover letter / Letter of intent addressing qualifications as they relate to stated criteria \u00b7 Curriculum Vitae \u00b7 Contact information for three references \u00b7 Unofficial transcripts Additional Information \u00b7 The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting universities. Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Chair, Department of Psychology Job Posting Number 2027007TTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division Department Psychology Position Description The College of Liberal Arts at Texas State University invites applications for the position of Chair of the Department of Psychology . The Chair of the Department of Psychology leads the largest department in the College of Liberal Arts. Responsibilities include: overseeing the curriculum, budget, and hiring of faculty and staff; long-range strategic planning and facilitating growth in line with departmental vision; and representing the department on college and university councils. For more information about the functions of department chairs at Texas State, visit https://policies.txst.edu/division-policies/academic-affairs/01-02-11.html . We seek a colleague who can foster academic excellence, strengthen and develop graduate programs, encourage interdisciplinary and engaged scholarship, and promote continued collegiality within the department. The department has a strong history of shared governance with a large and varied faculty, including both tenure-track and instructional-track faculty. The Chair holds a 12-month appointment expected to start July 15, 2027. The successful applicant will meet the requirements for tenure in the Department of Psychology, ideally at the rank of Professor, though highly qualified Associate Professors may be considered. About the University & Department Texas State University is a doctoral-granting university located in the burgeoning Austin-San Antonio corridor, the largest campus in the Texas State University System, and among the largest universities in the state. The Department of Psychology currently offers a B.A. and B.S. degree in Psychology, a M.A. in Psychological Research ( MAPR ), and undergraduate minors in general psychology, forensic psychology, sport psychology, and data analytics. The B.A. degree can be completed at the San Marcos campus, Round Rock campus, Quer\u00e9taro, Mexico, campus, or through our Accelerated Online program. The B.S. degree can be completed at the San Marcos campus, Round Rock campus, and Quer\u00e9taro, Mexico, campus. More information is available at www.psych.txst.edu . Required Qualifications Earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in Psychology or a closely related discipline (area of specialization open). Record of achievement in research, teaching, and service sufficient for appointment with tenure at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor at the time of appointment. Demonstrated administrative leadership experience in higher education or a comparable professional setting, including responsibilities related to strategic planning, budget management, personnel supervision, policy implementation, curriculum oversight, and/or academic program administration. Demonstrated evidence of successful mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students. The successful applicant will receive the appropriate rank and title based on university and department established standards. Preferred Qualifications Record of achievement in research, teaching, and service sufficient for appointment with tenure at the rank of Professor. Evidence of successful acquisition and management of externally funded projects. Demonstrated commitment to strengths-based management and transparency as a leader. Evidence of successful organizational and fiscal management practices consistent with managing and supporting a growing department and the strategic plans of the department, college, and university. Demonstrated commitment to supporting departmental cohesion that prioritizes the success of both teaching-focused and research-focused faculty. Ability to cultivate external community partnerships to support and grow department initiatives and programming. Demonstrated experience supporting or participating in APA accreditation and program review processes. Application Procedures Applications must be submitted through the Texas State University job opportunities website at https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58402 . For full consideration, application materials should be submitted by November 15, 2026 ; review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Required Application Documents Cover letter / Letter of intent addressing qualifications as they relate to stated criteria. Curriculum Vitae. Contact information for three references. Unofficial transcripts (all in one document). The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree-granting institutions prior to appointment. Proposed Start Date July 15, 2027 Posting Date 09/14/2026 Review Date 11/16/2026 Close Date 11/15/2026 Open Until Filled? Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, drug screening (if applicable), and employment eligibility verifications. Certain positions, including those with clinical responsibilities, require compliance with health, immunization, and other requirements mandated by affiliated clinical agencies. Employment and continued assignment in such roles are contingent upon meeting and maintaining these requirements. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58402 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD. in Psychology or a closely related field? Yes, I have a PhD. in Psychology or a closely related field. No, I do not have a PhD. in Psychology or a closely related field. Yes, ABD with a completion date prior to the listed start date. Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58416": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Philosophy (Ethics and Philosophy of Emerging Technologies)", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Philosophy (Ethics and Philosophy of Emerging Technologies) Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Assistant Professor of Philosophy (Ethics and Philosophy of Emerging Technologies) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Philosophy (Ethics and Philosophy of Emerging Technologies) Job Posting Number 2026087TTL Job Location Round Rock, San Marcos, Other - Online College/Division Department Philosophy Position Description The Department of Philosophy at Texas State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor to start Fall 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to be an effective undergraduate and graduate teacher, develop a productive research program, contribute to department and college initiatives and leadership (especially the Philosophy Dialogues), and to be committed to teaching lower-level philosophy courses as part of a core curriculum. Members of the department have secured funding through NSF , NEH , AAAS , Rethinking Priorities, and Humanities Texas in recent years. Typical teaching load is 3/3, with a 2/2 assigned for the first two years. Summer teaching is sometimes available, depending on student demand. The Department of Philosophy at Texas State University offers the B.A. in Philosophy; the B.A. in Religious Studies; the M.A. in Applied Philosophy and Ethics; undergraduate minors in Philosophy, Religious Studies, Value Studies, and Medical Humanities ; and graduate certificates in Professional Ethics , Ethics and Digital Technologies , and Environmental Leadership Engagement, and Ethics . Course assignments are based on expertise and departmental need, possibly including doctoral-level Responsible Conduct of Research/Research Ethics. Some teaching may be in evening courses or online. Members of the department\u2019s faculty regularly teach courses in 11 programs outside of our department: Latino/a Studies, African American Studies, Women\u2019s Studies, Sustainability Studies, Materials Science and Engineering, Physics, Education, History, Chemistry & Biochemistry, Undergraduate Research, and the Honors College The Department has 53 full-time faculty members in Spring 2026 (5 in Religious Studies, 46 in Philosophy, and 2 who teach in both disciplines), and teaches the largest number of undergraduate philosophy students of any public university in Texas, averaging over 9,000 students per year over the past six years. Departmental activities include the Philosophy Dialogues , a program of ~50 public-facing events each semester including lectures, films, readings, performances, and discussions; an active chapter of Phi Sigma Tau; an annual student symposium; a growing Religious Studies Student Organization; two student journals (Texas Philosophical and Stance); three professional journals; an Ethics Bowl team, and an International Business Ethics and Sustainability Case Competition team. PhD in Philosophy required by the time of appointment . ABD candidates please provide a letter from your committee chair verifying your anticipated completion before 1 August 2027. All positions are subject to availability of funds. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Philosophy by time of appointment. ( ABD applicants should provide a letter from your committee chair verifying anticipated completion before 1 August 2027). Previous teaching experience. Research and teaching specialization: Ethics and Philosophy of Emerging Technologies Teaching competence in: Philosophy/Ethics of Digital Technologies and Philosophy/Ethics of AI. Evidence of teaching excellence. Active research program. Evidence of professional or institutional service. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience in one or more of:Applied Philosophy, Bioethics/Medical Humanities, Environmental Philosophy, Experience teaching large classes (100+ students). Experience teaching or mentoring graduate students. Experience in interdisciplinary teaching or research. Experience in coordinating a speaker series, community engagement, or conference/symposia. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/53559 . To ensure full consideration, please submit the materials listed below before September 4, 2026: A letter of interest addressing how your work will contribute to new initiatives in applied or digital humanities to Dr. Craig Hanks, Chair of Search Committee. Current curriculum vitae. Research statement, including summary of any funded research, work in-progress, and future plans. Teaching statement (to include a discussion of general education). Evidence of teaching excellence. Two sample syllabi: A syllabus for one of our two 1000-level courses: PHIL 1305: Philosophy and Critical Thinking, or PHIL 1320: Ethics and Society; A Syllabus for a graduate or upper-level course in Philosophy or Ethics of Technology. Three \u2013 Five professional references including names, e-mail addresses, and telephone numbers. Letters of recommendation will be required prior to interviews. As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) \u2013 five (5) references. Please provide the names and email addresses for your references in the Reference Letter section of the employment application. When we need the letter, an automated email will be generated and sent to your references with instructions on how to attach the reference letter to your application through a confidential online portal. Applicants are strongly advised to remind their referees to respond to the letter request in a timely manner. If the letter of recommendation will be collected through Interfolio Dossier, please provide the specific Interfolio email in lieu of the references email. If a central office is responsible for responding to all reference letter requests in your department, please notify Dr. Hanks at craig.hanks@txstate.edu and Faculty and Academic Resources at facultyresources@txstate.edu . The selected candidate will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Proposed Start Date Fall 2027 Posting Date 06/09/2026 Review Date 09/08/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Legal Notices Texas State University is committed to a policy of non-discrimination and equal opportunity for all persons regardless of race, sex, color, religion, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal or state law in employment, educational programs, and activities and admissions. Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. This position may conduct research on critical infrastructure depending on the research focus of a hire. Consistent with the requirements of the State of Texas, individuals conducting research on critical infrastructure will be subject to pre-employment, and then subsequent routine background checks/cybersecurity screenings. Employment will at all times be contingent upon the successful completion of these screenings in accordance with State and University requirements. Reasonable Accommodation If you experience accessibility issues or require alternative formatting during the application process due to a disability or underlying condition, we request that you contact Talent Acquisition for assistance. A representative from Talent Acquisition will respond to you as soon as possible. Record Checks and Verifications Employment with Texas State University is contingent upon the outcome of record checks and verifications including, but not limited to, criminal history, driving records, education records, employment verifications, reference checks, and employment eligibility verifications. Eligibility for Employment In accordance with federal law, all new employees must complete the Form I-9 and provide acceptable documentation verifying their identity and authorization to work in the United States. Texas State University participates in E-Verify, and employment is contingent upon the successful verification of work authorization. Employees are required to maintain valid work authorization to satisfy the conditions of Form I9 at all times during their employment and the university makes no implicit or explicit promises to financially support visa or permanent residency applications. Why Work at Texas State? Texas State University is a large, student-centered public research institution serving more than 40,000 students across undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs in San Marcos and Round Rock. Classified as a Carnegie Doctoral University with High Research Activity (R2), TXST is actively advancing its ambitious Run to R1 strategy, demonstrating sustained growth in research activity, doctoral education, and scholarly impact. Faculty at TXST join a vibrant academic community of over 5,000 faculty and staff committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service. The university offers a collaborative, supportive environment, and interdisciplinary scholarship. Outstanding faculty are drawn to TXST for the opportunity to make a meaningful impact\u2014advancing research, mentoring a growing student body, and helping shape the future of a rapidly growing research university. Quick Link https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/53559 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (all in one document) Other Required Documents Syllabi Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents DD 214/DD1300 Veteran's Preference List of References Samples of Scholarly Work/Research Additional Document Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in philosophy or ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date? Yes, I have a Ph.D. in philosophy. Yes, ABD with anticipated completion prior to start date. No. * What is your schedule availability? Days/Nights; Days of the Week; Location (e.g., San Marcos, Round Rock, online courses, etc.) (Open Ended Question) Office of Human Resources 231 N. Guadalupe St. San Marcos, Texas 78666 Phone: 512.245.2557 Fax: 512.245.1942 Email: hr@txstate.edu Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/58385": {"title": "Nontenure Faculty Pool - Music", "description": "Texas State University Applicant Portal | Nontenure Faculty Pool - Music Skip to Main Content Job Opportunities at Texas State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Faculty and Academic Resources Human Resources Student Nontenure Faculty Pool - Music Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Information Posting Information Position Title Nontenure Faculty Pool - Music Job Posting Number 2026139NTL Job Location San Marcos College/Division College of Fine Arts and Communication Department/School School of Music Position Description The School of Music seeks to develop a pool of candidates for possible temporary/non-tenured faculty to teach music courses. New hires will join a nationally recognized department with a dynamic faculty dedicated to a collaborative and innovative approach to teaching undergraduate and graduate students. Temporary/non-tenured faculty are appointed to teach one to four courses per semester. Teaching appointments are based upon student demand on a semester-by-semester basis. Eligibility for annual reappointment is contingent upon satisfactory annual performance evaluations during the term period, in addition to continuity of funding and departmental need. This posting is for the fall 2026, spring 2027, and summer 2026/2027 semesters. Please note that this posting is not intended to convey that such a need currently exists. Applicants applying for a pool faculty position will be available to the departmental search committee for consideration in case the need arises. All positions are subject to availability of funds. Required Qualifications Specific educational requirements vary by position, but a minimum of a bachelor\u2019s degree or commensurate experience is required. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in music, or equivalent professional experience, and/or prior teaching experience is preferred. Application Procedures Only applications submitted through the Texas State University website will be accepted and considered: https://jobs.hr.txstate.edu/postings/57280 . Interested individuals should submit the following: Current CV, Cover letter outlining specific academic and professional experiences relevant for appointment, Statement of teaching philosophy, Unofficial transcripts (all transcripts should be in one document). As part of our application process, we are requesting contact information for three (3) academic references who can provide information about the applicant\u2019s skills and experiences. Please provide the names and email addresses for your academic references in the List of References section of the employment application. Candidates selected for hire will be required to provide official transcripts from all degree granting universities. Additional documents might be required for specific positions, please contact music@txstate.edu for additional guidance specific to open positions. Type of Position Temporary Full-Time or Part-Time Proposed Start Date FY 27 Posting Date 06/09/2026 Review Date 06/30/2026 Close Date 05/31/2027 Open Until Filled? No 